n – A photographic engagement, Atelier Akim, Berlin, Germany2005 Pergamon, Galerie du XXe Siècle, Paris, [&hellip;]'),(243,53,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(244,53,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25169\" class=\"elementor elementor-25169\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5f02026 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"5f02026\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e283fda e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"e283fda\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-dcbb4ac elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"dcbb4ac\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-99ed6d4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"99ed6d4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in 1968, Swiss, Lives in Berlin, Germany</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7f28467 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"7f28467\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5ccdc77 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"5ccdc77\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7c50d0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"a7c50d0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1985 -1990 Cornell University, NY Bachelor of Arts (Comp. Lit. &amp; Art History)</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b980b51 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"b980b51\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-808ef95 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"808ef95\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-518aced elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"518aced\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3abfe5d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"3abfe5d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2014 Seeking Al-Tawhid in Andalucia, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2013 Seeking Al-Tawhid in Andalucia, JAMM Gallery, Kuwait<br />2009 Rodin – A photographic engagement, Atelier Akim, Berlin, Germany<br />2005 Pergamon, Galerie du XXe Siècle, Paris, France<br />2004 Akim Monet – Hommage à Gaudi, Maruani &amp; Noirhomme Gallery, Belgium<br />2004 Hommage à Gaudi 5, rue de la Muse, Geneva, Switzerland<br />2003 Passage to India, Muestra 2 – Art Fair, Mexico City – Carosso Fine Art, NYC<br />2003 The Space Between, Book presentation sponsored by Collection Deutsche<br />Bank benefit sale for « Free Arts for Abused Children, NYC »<br />2002 Passage to India, Carosso Fine Art, New York, USA</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a70a24 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"4a70a24\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b590558 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b590558\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Photographic Projects				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-523d915 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"523d915\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2014 Homage Rebrandt Bugatti, Alte Nationalgalerie, Berlin (Germany)<br />2010 Life in Death – the Catacombs, Palermo, (Italy)<br />2009 Rodin – a photographic engagement, Musée Rodin, Paris (France)<br />2006 Seeking Al Tawhid, Andalucia (Spain)<br />Corrida La Goyesca, Ronda (Spain)<br />In the Vatican Gardens, Rome (Italy)<br />2004 Villa Adriana, Tivoli (Italy)<br />Pergamon, Berlin (Germany)<br />The Caves – a meditation, Vallorbe (Switzerland)<br />2001 Exotic Flowers, Bali (Indonesia) &amp; NYC<br />2000 Homage to Gaudi, Barcelona (Spain)<br />1992 Passage to India, Countrywide (India)</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3b800bd e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"3b800bd\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e736ecb e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"e736ecb\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-0a225fa elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"0a225fa\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Corporate Collections				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2b59378 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2b59378\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2013 Gatehouse Bank, London<br />2004 Deutsche Bank Collection, Frankfurt<br />– Trading Floor, 60 Wall Street, New York</p></div></div>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-90dedf6 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"90dedf6\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3f05b90 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3f05b90\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bibliography				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-03cacf5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"03cacf5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2005 Hilarie M. Sheets, Pergamon, Exhibition catalogue, Paris<br />2003 Andres Serrano, Akim Monet, Hilarie M. Sheets, The space between, New<br />York: Infinite Point Press</p></div></div>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b187b58 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"b187b58\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-986660b e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"986660b\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9e47436 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"9e47436\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Artist Residency				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d33b4ba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d33b4ba\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2005 University of Maine School of Fine Arts – Department of New Media</p></div></div>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c572fd1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"c572fd1\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(245,53,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(246,53,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(247,53,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(248,53,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(249,53,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-53\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(250,56,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-al-braithwaite.jpg'),(251,56,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:670;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:4:\"file\";s:33:\"2026/08/artist-al-braithwaite.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:71290;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:33:\"artist-al-braithwaite-196x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:196;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9980;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:33:\"artist-al-braithwaite-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5113;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(252,55,'_thumbnail_id','292'),(253,55,'portrait','292'),(254,55,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(255,55,'origin','BIO Born in 1979, Rinteln, W.Germany Al Braithwaite is a contemporary artist from London, who works across a variety of disciplines including sculpture, assemblage, found material and installation. His work fits into a tradition of conceptual art, recalling Dada, Surrealism, Fluxus, and aspects of Orphism. Al co-founded The Offscreen Group with writer Henry Hemming in [&hellip;]'),(256,55,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(257,55,'intro','BIO Born in 1979, Rinteln, W.Germany Al Braithwaite is a contemporary artist from London, who works across a variety of disciplines including sculpture, assemblage, found material and installation. His work fits into a tradition of conceptual art, recalling Dada, Surrealism, Fluxus, and aspects of Orphism. Al co-founded The Offscreen Group with writer Henry Hemming in [&hellip;]'),(258,55,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(259,55,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25200\" class=\"elementor elementor-25200\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-964a694 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"964a694\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3013075 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"3013075\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-da9188f elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"da9188f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-87d26ed elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"87d26ed\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in 1979, Rinteln, W.Germany</p><p>Al Braithwaite is a contemporary artist from London, who works across a variety of disciplines including sculpture, assemblage, found material and installation. His work fits into a tradition of conceptual art, recalling Dada, Surrealism, Fluxus, and aspects of Orphism.</p><p>Al co-founded The Offscreen Group with writer Henry Hemming in 2002. The group worked in a number of countries on a low-budget model like the Beat poets, the Black Audio Film Collective or the Russian group AES+F. During its time the group was joined by feminist filmmaker Georgie Weedon and curator Stephen A. Stapleton, co-founder of Edge of Arabia. From 2005 Al pursued more solo work, continuing the same low-budget model but for his own purposes. An interest in considering different contexts led him to places like Ground Zero, United States, and Trinidad in the West Indies, which have both impacted his work. Hybrid textures play a significant role in his practice.</p><p>His piece The Limes Installation (2014) showed to small audiences at Alice Yard, Port of Spain, a non-profit project space with an ongoing residency programme, in its seventh year.</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-fb65198 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"fb65198\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7502b76 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"7502b76\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3e05976 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3e05976\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8394a99 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8394a99\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Museum No.1: Hizbollah’s Caviar at Rose Issa Projects, London (2009);<br />Twinned Towers at Leila Heller Gallery, New York (2011);<br />Transgressions at XVA Gallery, Dubai (2012).</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-561726d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"561726d\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-0921578 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"0921578\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-010f14b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"010f14b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Works				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c78deb9 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c78deb9\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>The Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan bin Khalifa Al Nahyan Private Collection, Abu Dhabi;<br />The Salsali Private Museum (SPM), Dubai;<br />The Sheikha Paula al-Sabah Private Collection, Kuwait;<br />The Moez Ahamed Jamal Private Collection, Zurich;<br />The British Council Collection, Tehran;<br />The Art Fund Collection, London;<br />The Farook Collection, Dubai;<br />Vasili Tsereteli Collection, Moscow;<br />The British Museum Collection, London.</p></div></div>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(260,55,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(261,55,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(262,55,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(263,55,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(264,55,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-55\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(265,58,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-alejandra.jpg'),(266,58,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:731;s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"2026/08/artist-alejandra.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:48740;s:5:\"sizes\";a:5:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"artist-alejandra-300x214.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:214;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:7303;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"artist-alejandra-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4398;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"artist-alejandra-768x548.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:548;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:29114;}s:12:\"xva-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"artist-alejandra-1000x731.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1000;s:6:\"height\";i:731;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:49185;}s:8:\"xva-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"artist-alejandra-900x731.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:731;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:47698;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(267,57,'_thumbnail_id','289'),(268,57,'portrait','289'),(269,57,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(270,57,'origin','Alejandra sees the universe through the matrix of multiculturalism, and this has gifted her with a special perception of the world. Over twenty years she has focused on the arts and participated in specialty courses, by international experts to enrich herself.'),(271,57,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(272,57,'intro','Alejandra sees the universe through the matrix of multiculturalism, and this has gifted her with a special perception of the world. Over twenty years she has focused on the arts and participated in specialty courses, by international experts to enrich herself.'),(273,57,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(274,57,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25247\" class=\"elementor elementor-25247\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in 1971 in Caborca, Mexico. She has lived in Geneva, Switzerland, Sendai, Japan and currently resides in Dubai.</p><p>Alejandra sees the universe through the matrix of multiculturalism, and this has gifted her with a special perception of the world. Over twenty years she has focused on the arts and participated in specialty courses, by international experts to enrich herself. A very important period of her artistic career was the one while living in Japan – land of silence, beauty and Zen – where she presented a Solo exhibition. She enjoys working with a wide range of materials like old wood, cement, recycled metal and everyday objects. Alejandra’s sculptures and commissioned art installations have been presented and awarded in Solo and Collective Exhibitions in prestigious venues as: The regional Museum of Anthropology and History and at the city theater of La Paz Baja California Sur, Mexico; In Universities, Galleries and Art Fairs across Mexico; Port Louis, Mauritius; New York, USA; Beirut, Lebanon; as well as across UAE in Dubai, Ras Al Khaima, Um Al Quwain and Abu Dhabi.</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9323c6e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9323c6e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-696a287 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"696a287\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3082519 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3082519\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5b42980 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5b42980\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2019 Um Al Quwain Ministry of Culture Center, “Desert Origins”, Um Al Quwain, UAE;<br />2013, Public Art Installation, Museo Regional de Antropología e Historia, “Movimiento Ancestral”, La Paz Baja California Sur, México;<br />2011 Public Art Installation, Universidad Autónoma de Baja California Sur, “Mundialmente Unidos por Japón”, La Paz, B.C.S., Mexico;<br />2010 Birdo Space Gallery, “My Senses”, Minatomachi Shiogama, Miyagi, Japan;<br />2009 Universidad Autónoma de Baja California Sur “Nostalgia”, La Paz Baja California Sur, México;<br />2009 Public Art installation, Tecnológico de La Paz, “Equilibrio en Desafío”, La Paz, Baja California Sur, México;<br />2008 Universidad Del Valle de Atemajac, “Alejandra Palos Ortega”, Guadalajara, Jalisco, México;<br />2002 Teatro de la Ciudad, “Recordar la Luz”, La Paz, Baja California, México.</p>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b51338 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9b51338\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-310d379 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child\" data-id=\"310d379\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n					<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-004ddf5 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"004ddf5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b3a5f10 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"b3a5f10\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d8d236f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d8d236f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>2024 Ajman Museum , Al Murabbaa Arts festival, Ajman , UAE<br />2024 XVA Gallery, “Fronde Science Summer Show”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2024 ZeeArts, One and OnlyRoyal Mirage, “7th Edition Art Connects Women”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2023 Cultural Centre Umm Al Quwain, “UAQ Arts Festival 2023”, Umm Al Quwain, UAE;<br />2022 Embassy of Mexico, “From the UAE to Mexico”, Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2021 The Meydan Hotel, “Dubai Art Expo” by Artissima, Dubai, UAE;<br />2021 Embassy of Mexico, “An Introspective look at Nature, its colors and textures”, Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2021 Al Jaziraah Al Hamra Heritage Village, 9th edition Ras Al Khaima Fine Arts Festival, Ras Al Khaima, UAE;<br />2020 Tashkeel, “Covid Conversations”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2020 Arte in Regola and Artissima Art Gallery, “Italia In Arte Exhibition”, Rome, Italy;<br />2020 Alliance Francaise Art Exhibition by the Museum of Americas, Introspection, Dubai, UAE;<br />2020 Dubai Opera, within the framework of the conference “Each for Equal”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2020 One And Only Royal Mirage, Exhibition by Zeearts Gallery Art Connects Women, Dubai, UAE;<br />2020 Central Park Towers, Exhibition by Gallery Arabesque “Women in Art” Dubai, UAE;<br />2020 Cultural Centre Umm Al Quwain, “UAQ Art Festival 2020” Umm Al Quwain, UAE;<br />2020 Embassy of Mexico Mexican Art in United Arab Emirates, Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2020 Al Jaziraat Al Hamra, Ras Al Khaima Fine Arts Festival, Ras Al Khaima, UAE;<br />2019 Unbox Art Space, Chance, Allowing Chance to Dictate Art, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Central Park Towers, Common Ground Exhibition, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Alliance Francaise, Art Exhibition by Museum of The Americas, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Archiade Atelier Dubai Design District, Art Unity by Artissima, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Workshop for teenagers, Um Al Quwain Ministry of Culture Center, Um Al Quwain, UAE;<br />2019 Seaside Arena, Zeearts Gallery at Beirut Art Fair, Beirut, Lebanon;<br />2019 Caudan Arts Centre, “Mauritius International Art Fair” Port Louis, Mauritius;<br />2019 Dubai International Art Centre, gallery 76, “Summer Salon Exhibition”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 World Trade Centre, “World Art Dubai”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Dubai International Art Centre, gallery 76, “Art Week”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Pier 90, “Artexpo New York” New York, USA;<br />2019 Etihad Modern Art Gallery, ” ART SOUQ” Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2019 One &amp; Only Royal Mirage Grand Gallery, ” Islam and Tolerance” Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 One and Only Royal Mirage, International Women´s Day” Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 IGH Cassells Al Barsha Hotel, ” Beyond Borders”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2019 Ras Al Khaimah National Museum, “7th Annual Ras Al Khaimah Fine Arts Festival”, Ras Al Khaimah, UAE<br />2019 Al Jazirah Al Hamra “7th Annual Ras Al Khaimah Fine Arts Festival”, Ras Al Khaimah, UAE<br />2018 Art Hub Abu Dhabi, “UAE National Day Exhibition” Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2018 Sorbonne University-Abu Dhabi, “Zayed and his Legacy”, Abu Dhabi, UAE;<br />2018 Gallery 76 DIAC, “63rd Members Exhibition”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2018 Ahmedia Art Gallery, “Heart of Heritage”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2018 Gallery 76 DIAC, “Celebrating Ramadan”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2018 One and Only Royal Mirage Hotel, “Press for Progress”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2018 The National Museum of Ras Al Khaimah, “RAK Fine Arts Festival”, Ras Al Khaima, UAE;<br />2017, Gallery 76 DIAC, “62nd Members Exhibition”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2017 Jumeirah Beach Hotel, La Parrilla Restaurant, “Art Unity”, Dubai, UAE;<br />2017 Teatro de la Ciudad, “Fine Arts End of the Year Exhibition” La Paz, Baja California Sur, Mexico;<br />2009 Colegio de Jalisco “Celebrating Freedom From Addictions”, Zapopan, Jalisco, Mexico;<br />2008 Eusebio Francisco Kino Gallery, “Bidimension,Cuerpo y Cotidianidad” Hermosillo, Sonora, Mexico;<br />2008 Rabid Rabbits Gallery, “Sacred Spaces” Ajijic, Jalisco, Mexico;<br />2008 Centro Cultural Axixic, “Day of the Dead” Ajijic, Jalisco, Mexico;<br />2008 Public Art installation Book fair, “Leer para Crecer”, Hermosillo, Sonora, Mexico;<br />2008 Colegio de Jalisco “Celebrating Freedom from Addictions”, Zapopan, Jalisco, Mexico;<br />2008 Familia #Public Art Riqui-Ran Child Center. La Pax Baja California Sur, Mexico. Donated 2017</p></div><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d19d98 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4d19d98\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>hortlisted for The Art Circle Award in January 2024<br />Nominated for The Salama bint Hamdan Emerging Artists Fellowship 2022 and 2023.</p></div></div></div>								</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(275,57,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(276,57,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(277,57,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(278,57,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(279,57,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-57\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(280,60,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-halim.jpg'),(281,60,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:759;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"2026/08/artist-halim.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:82762;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"artist-halim-222x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:222;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:12304;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"artist-halim-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5964;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(282,59,'_thumbnail_id','277'),(283,59,'portrait','277'),(284,59,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(285,59,'origin','BIO Born in Erbil, Kurdistan – Iraq. Lives in Florence, Italy. An international artist and a citizen of the world, Azad Nanakeli has focused his visual pattern on a multi-layered artistic discourse, at the crossroads between an impressive variety of media: painting, photography, video, installation, and an equally powerful narrative, which gives all his work [&hellip;]'),(286,59,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(287,59,'intro','BIO Born in Erbil, Kurdistan – Iraq. Lives in Florence, Italy. An international artist and a citizen of the world, Azad Nanakeli has focused his visual pattern on a multi-layered artistic discourse, at the crossroads between an impressive variety of media: painting, photography, video, installation, and an equally powerful narrative, which gives all his work [&hellip;]'),(288,59,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(289,59,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25294\" class=\"elementor elementor-25294\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in Erbil, Kurdistan – Iraq. Lives in Florence, Italy.</p><p>An international artist and a citizen of the world, Azad Nanakeli has focused his visual pattern on a multi-layered artistic discourse, at the crossroads between an impressive variety of media: painting, photography, video, installation, and an equally powerful narrative, which gives all his work an almost spiritual touch of coherence and unity. Born in Erbil, today part of the Kurdistan Autonomous Region in Iraq, currently living in Florence, Italy, Azad illustrated his trans-national mix of identity in around a hundred of international exhibitions, culminating in three editions of the Venice Biennale: the Kurdish pavilion in 2009, the Iraqi pavilion in 2011 and the Iranian pavilion in 2015.</p><p>Highlighted Memory, his solo exhibition in Dubai, was an invitation to an overview of Nanakeli’s major topics of reflection and a highly representative illustration of his innovative technique based on the overlapping of narrative and mixed media layers. The exhibition proposed a new frame where the artist could freely develop his own timeless connections between personal and trans-individual experiences, between the past and the present, between memory and identity. In Nanakeli’s view, art becomes a recording and a critical process, able to contribute to a comprehension of the social role and the meaning of the artistic practice, proposing a series of reflections on how much art can contribute to the configuration of the modern world representation; interrogating itself at the same time on how the artist can make a correlation between the political reality and the social dramas through their artistic representation. In every layer of pictorial, or sound, or video matter of his works, the artist turns himself into a sort of archaeologist, able to dig and unveil the ‘ghost’ and unexpected faces of the personal and collective experience: it is as if, together with the artist, the viewer would enter his artworks from the back-door of the memory and have access in this way to a privileged and magical storytelling.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9323c6e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9323c6e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-696a287 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"696a287\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3082519 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3082519\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5b42980 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5b42980\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>1983 Lithographic Arts Diploma, International School of Graphic Arts Il Bisonte, Florence, Italy.<br />1979 Degree from the Academy of Fine Arts, Florence, Italy.<br />1975 Degree from the Institute of Fine Arts, Baghdad, Iraq.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b51338 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9b51338\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-310d379 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"310d379\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-004ddf5 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"004ddf5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b3a5f10 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"b3a5f10\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d8d236f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d8d236f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>2022 World Gallery, Erbil, Kurdistan, Iraq.<br />2019 Media Hall Gallery, Erbil, Kurdistan, Iraq.<br />2018 50 Minutes Video Arte, Culturale Art Center of Erbil – Cittadel, Kurdistan.<br />2017 Highlighted Memory, XVA Gallery, Dubai, UAE.<br />2017 Mag Gallery, Como, Italy.<br />2016 3rd Edition International Contemporary Art, Palazzo del Podestà, Gipsoteca Libero Andreotti, Pescia, Italy.<br />2016 Galleria Civico Otto, Pescia, Italy<br />2016 Hinterland Gallery, Wien, Austria.<br />2016 Karsi Sanat Gallery, Istanbul, Turkey.<br />2015 Museo Moca, Yinchuan, China.<br />2015 Museo Vignoli, Seregno, Milan, Italy.<br />2015 Biblioteca Nazionale Universitaria, Turin, Italy.<br />2015 Museo Storico Nazionale, Tirana, Albania.<br />2014 Museo Villa Vecchia, Villa Dario Pamphili, Rome, Italy.<br />2014 Amed Sanat Galerisi Sümerpark, Diyarbakir, Turkey.<br />2013 The Grate Game, Pavilion of Iran, 56th Venice Biennale, Venice, Italy.<br />2013 Un Mare d’Inchiostro, Galleria del Accademia delle Arti del Disegno, Florence, Italy.<br />2013 Serdem Gallery, Sulaymaniyah, Kurdistan, Iraq.<br />2012 Palazzo Granafei, Nervegna, Brindisi, Italy.<br />2012 Media Gallery, Erbil, Kurdistan, Iraq.<br />2012 Barocco Austero Presenze nel nostro tempo, Museo Regionale del Barocco, Noto, Italy.<br />2011 Mare di Cinema Arabi, Fondazione Horcynus Orca, Messina, Italy.<br />2011 Wounded Water, Pavilion of Iraq, 54th Venice Biennale, Venice, Italy.<br />2011 Antiche Cucine dell’ex Monastero dei Benedettini, Catania, Italy.<br />2010 Visioni Irachena, Palazzo Strozzi, Florence, Italy.<br />2010 The Berlin Wall Media Art, Petro Marko Theater, Valona, Albania.<br />2010 Illumination, Installation performance, Studio Azad, Florence, Italy.<br />2009 Planet-K, 53rd Venice Biennale, Venice, Italy.<br />2009 Homage to Kamel Shiaa Abdullah, Bozar, Brussels, Belgium.<br />2008 Istanbul Art Fair, Istanbul, Turkey.<br />2006 Poetronica, Cinema Teatro Moderno, Lastra a Signa, Florence, Italy.<br />2005 La mossa delle idee, Videodays 2, Sala Santa Rita, Rome, Italy.<br />2004 Tracce Fuoricentro live, Fuori Centro, Livorno, Italy.<br />2004 La mossa delle idee, Videodays, Cinema Alfieri Atelier, Florence, Italy.<br />2004 Cinema Spazio Uno, Florence – Italy<br />2003 Outlook, National Museum, Krakow, Poland.<br />2002 Grenzenlos, Volkshalle im Wiener Rathaus, Wien, Austria.<br />2001 Wayfarer, Galerie Anton Meier S.A., Geneva, Switzerland.<br />1999 Borup Højskole Art Gallery, Copenhagen, Denmark.<br />1998 Stefanini Gallery, Florence, Italy.<br />1998 Pilonova Gallery, Ajdovscina, Slovenia.<br />1997 Dvorni Trg, Ljubljana, Slovenia.<br />1996 Under anden himmel, Il Salone Gallery, Copenhagen, Denmark.<br />1996 Duca Gallery, Vipava, Slovenia.<br />1996 Eclisse Gallery, Locarno, Switzerland.<br />1996 Planque Gallery, Lausanne, Switzerland.<br />1994 L’Escale Gallery, Brussels, Belgium.<br />1994 De Muzerije Art Center, Hertogenbosch, The Netherlands.<br />1994 Artforum Gallery, Wien, Austria.</p></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(290,59,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(291,59,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(292,59,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(293,59,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(294,59,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-59\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(295,62,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-charlie.jpg'),(296,62,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:670;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/08/artist-charlie.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:106763;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-charlie-196x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:196;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10778;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-charlie-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5403;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(297,61,'_thumbnail_id','274'),(298,61,'portrait','274'),(299,61,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(300,61,'origin','BIO Born in 1973, South Africa Barbara Wildenboer was born in Pretoria, South Africa in 1973. She received her Bachelor of Visual Arts from UNISA and completed her Masters in Fine Art (with distinction) at the Michaelis School of Art at the University of Cape Town in 2007. She currently lives and works in Cape [&hellip;]'),(301,61,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(302,61,'intro','BIO Born in 1973, South Africa Barbara Wildenboer was born in Pretoria, South Africa in 1973. She received her Bachelor of Visual Arts from UNISA and completed her Masters in Fine Art (with distinction) at the Michaelis School of Art at the University of Cape Town in 2007. She currently lives and works in Cape [&hellip;]'),(303,61,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(304,61,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25315\" class=\"elementor elementor-25315\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in 1973, South Africa</p><p>Barbara Wildenboer was born in Pretoria, South Africa in 1973. She received her Bachelor of Visual Arts from UNISA and completed her Masters in Fine Art (with distinction) at the Michaelis School of Art at the University of Cape Town in 2007. She currently lives and works in Cape Town, South Africa.</p><p>Barbara Wildenboer’s work mostly consists of collage, photo/paper-construction, and digitally animated photographic sculpture. She uses a combination of analogue and digital processes to create work which explores different phenomena such as temporality, fractal geometry, and the interconnectedness of all living things. Wildenboer exposes the connections between a myriad of life forms: from the microscopic to the immense. Her main focus is on environmental aesthetics, seeing this as something that not only encompasses natural territories, but also extends to human interaction within the natural realm.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9323c6e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9323c6e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-696a287 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"696a287\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3082519 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3082519\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5b42980 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5b42980\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2007: MFA (with distinction), Michaelis School of Art, UCT.<br />2003: Bachelor of Visual Arts, UNISA.<br />1996: BA (Ed) with majors in English literature and Psychology, University of Pretoria. 2003: Bachelor of Visual Arts, UNISA.</p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b51338 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9b51338\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-310d379 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"310d379\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-004ddf5 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"004ddf5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				 Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-021dad8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"021dad8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d8d236f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d8d236f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2022: LOOT, This Is Not A White Cube Gallery, Lisbon, Portugal.<br />2020: Super/Natural, Everard Read Gallery /CIRCA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2020: Retrospective exhibition – Online, Festival artist for the Klein Karoo Arts Festival, Oudshoorn, South Africa.<br />2020: Library of the Infinitesimally Small and Unimaginably Large II, XVA Gallery, Dubai, UAE.<br />2019: Folly, Everard Read Gallery, London, UK.<br />2018: Eros / Thanatos, Everard Read Gallery, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2017: The Invisible Gardener, Everard Read Gallery /CIRCA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2016: Mythematics, Mcontemporary, Sydney, Australia.<br />2015: Something Rather Than Nothing, The Cat Street Gallery, Hong Kong.<br />2014: The Lotus Eaters, The Reservoir Gallery, Oliewenhuis, Bloemfontein, South Africa, William Humphreys Museum, Kimberley, South Africa, North West University, Potchefstroom, South Africa.<br />2013: Disjecta Membra, Amelia Johnson Contemporary, Hong Kong.<br />2012: Canaries in the Coalmine, ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town and Aardklop, Potchefstroom, South Africa.<br />2011: Library of the Infinitesimally Small and Unimaginably Large, ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2008: Present Absence/Absent Presence, ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2008:Vanitas, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2006: Everyday Alchemy, Darat al Funun, Khalid Shoman Foundation, Amman, Jordan.</p></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4124fb1 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4124fb1\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Awards				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b3a5f10 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"b3a5f10\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d8d236f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d8d236f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2018: Hannacc Residence for Arts, Barcelona<br />2016: L’Air Arts Residency, at L’Atelier sur Seine, Fontainebleau, France<br />2013: Rimbun Dahan Residency (Penang, Malaysia, 2013)<br />2011 Public Vote Prize<br />2011 African Art Prize<br />2006 Maclver Scholarship<br />2005/6 KW Johnstone Scholarship<br />2005/6 Jules Kramer Award<br />2005/6 Harry Crossley Scholarship<br />2002 Overall winner Vuleka Art Award, South Africa<br />2000 Merit award winner New Signatures, South Africa</p></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3d70169 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"3d70169\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c41a807 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"c41a807\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ee3e522 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ee3e522\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: CODA Paper Art 2021, CODA museum, Apeldoorn, The Netherlands.<br />2021: OASIS -25th anniversary exhibition, Everard Read Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2021: Either the world is crowded with garbage or our memories, Golubitskoe Art Foundation, Golubitskaya, Russia.<br />2021: Conversations, Everard Read Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2021: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2017-2021: Cut Up /Cut Out, travelling Museum Exhibition, Bellevue Arts Museum, WA (June 30 – Oct. 20, 2017) Huntsville Museum of Art, AL (Nov. 19 – Feb. 11, 2018), Pensacola Museum of Art, FL (March 2 – June 17, 2018) Ellen Noël Art Museum, Odessa, TX (July 19 – Oct. 14, 2018) Foosaner Art Museum, Melbourne, FL (Nov. 10 – Feb. 3, 2019) Woodson Art Museum, Wausau, WI (Mar. 2 – May 26, 2019), Amarillo Museum of Art in Amarillo, TX (July 6 -September 15, 2019), Lamont Gallery in Exeter, NH (Jan 21- March 4, 2020), Carnegie Arts Center in Turlock, CA (Oct 30 -January 3, 2021), USA.<br />2020: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2020: Tiny Treasures, Everard Read Gallery, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2018: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2017: Booknesses: South African Artists’ Books – FADA Gallery, As part of the BOOKNESSESS COLLOQUIEM held at the University of Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2017: By the Book, Kaller Fine Arts, Washington DC, USA.<br />2017: Reality Check, Everard Read Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2017: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2016: This is Not a Book, The San Jose Institute of Contemporary Art, California, USA.<br />2016: Surface and Subtext, Everard Read Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2016: -nano Barnard Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2016/2015: Map of the New Art – Imago Mundi – Luciano Benetton Collection, Isola di San Giorgio Maggiore, Venezia, Italy and New York, USA.<br />2016: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2016: Lush, SMAC Gallery, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2015: Ten years of Artists Books, A collection of artists’ books curated for the Brooklyn Public Library, New York, USA.<br />2015: Homage, Everard Read, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2015: Picture &amp; Paper, Barnard Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2015: The Spiritual in the Material, Lizamore and Associates Gallery, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2015: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2015: The Artist as Author, Klein Karoo Nasionale Kunstefees, Oudshoorn, South Africa.<br />2015: Empire, Everard Read, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2014: Butterflies in my Stomach, XVA Gallery, Al Fahidi, Dubai, UAE.<br />2014: Capital: Contemporary, Fried Contemporary, Pretoria, South Africa.<br />2014: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2013: Crossing the Divide Erdmann Contemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2013: Wonder Works, The Space, Hong Kong, HK.<br />2012: Conversations, Sydney, Australia.<br />2012: Clover Aardklop Arts Festival, Potcheftstroom, South Africa.<br />2011: Implemented Environments, Brundyn &amp; Gonsalves, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Conceptual Matters (part II), ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: The Mysteries and Mechanics of Perception, iArt, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Es(Cape), Pretoria Kunsvereniging, Pretoria, South Africa.<br />2010: Return to the Land, Klein Karoo Kunstefees, Oudshoorn, South Africa.<br />2010: Matters Conceptually(part I), ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Reading between the lines, US Gallery, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2009: 3d Riwaq Biennale, Birzeit, Palestine.<br />2008-2009: Construct: Beyond the Documentary Photograph (Travelling exhibition) Unisa Gallery, Pretoria, KZN Gallery, Durban, Nelson Mandela Metropolitan Gallery, Port Elizabeth, Grahamstown Art Festival (Main show), Grahamstown, Goethe Institute, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2008: Print 08: Myth, Memory and the Archive, Bell-Roberts Gallery, Woodstock, South Africa.<br />2007: Greenhouse, Bell-Roberts Gallery, Lourensford estate, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2007: Critic and Committee’s Choice, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2007: Come, Michaelis Gallery, Cape Town, KZNSA, Durban, South Africa.<br />2007: Fest, Durbanville Cultural Centre, Durbanville, South Africa.<br />2005: Absolut Finale, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2005: FINDING YOU (Collaborative exhibition of ceramic installation), AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2004: Absolut Moment, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2004: Exfoliate (A collaborative printmaking exhibition), ArtB, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2003: Trilogy, Sanlam Gallery, ArtB, Durbanville Cultural Centre, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2003: Old and New (Selected old and new works from the Sanlam Collection), Sanlam gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2002: Absolut Voyeur, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(305,61,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(306,61,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(307,61,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(308,61,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(309,61,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-61\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(310,64,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-hussein.jpg'),(311,64,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:337;s:6:\"height\";i:667;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/08/artist-hussein.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:51910;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-hussein-152x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:152;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9571;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-hussein-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5268;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(312,63,'_thumbnail_id','267'),(313,63,'portrait','267'),(314,63,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(315,63,'origin','For over twenty years, Charlie Koolhaas’ exhibitions have been immersive landscapes you can enter and explore – places where flat images are folded into three-dimensional structures offering infinite perspectives.'),(316,63,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(317,63,'intro','For over twenty years, Charlie Koolhaas’ exhibitions have been immersive landscapes you can enter and explore – places where flat images are folded into three-dimensional structures offering infinite perspectives.'),(318,63,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(319,63,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25350\" class=\"elementor elementor-25350\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				about the artist				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>For over twenty years, Charlie Koolhaas’ exhibitions have been immersive landscapes you can enter and explore – places where flat images are folded into three-dimensional structures offering infinite perspectives. Charlie has authored various books that tell sociological stories by merging her images and writing into unified narratives. In 2020 she released her book City Lust, which combines writing and photography to take the viewer on a journey through the global economy. Her recently launched Foto-Couture, which makes her prints wearable, further frees her photographs from the boundaries of art institutions allowing them to enter the world where their meaning continues to evolve. Charlie has taught media theory and photography in various academic institutions such as Eindhoven School of design, TUDelft and the Sandberg Academy, and she has been a visiting lecturer at Harvard Graduate School of Design, ETH Zurich and The Architectural Association London.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(320,63,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(321,63,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(322,63,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(323,63,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(324,63,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-63\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(325,66,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-halim-1.jpg'),(326,66,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:759;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/08/artist-halim-1.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:82762;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-halim-1-222x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:222;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:12304;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"artist-halim-1-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5964;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s: