t elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				About the Artist				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>B. 1939 D. 2014</p><p>Moussa Tiba studied at the Beirut Fine Arts Institute and later pursued further education in London, Rome, and other regions, exploring various artistic mediums. His style transitioned from figuration to abstraction in the 1970s, with watercolor becoming central to his work. Tiba’s art reflects a fusion of Western and Eastern influences, focusing on themes of creation, peace, and the regeneration of life.</p><p>Tiba’s work has been exhibited internationally in Lebanon, France, Germany, Norway, Egypt, Kuwait, and Brazil. His pieces are held in major collections, including the Musée des Beaux-Arts in Chartres, the Institut du Monde Arabe in Paris, and UNESCO in Beirut. His family home in Qana has been converted into a museum dedicated to his art and also displays works by other prominent artists.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(385,72,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(386,72,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(387,72,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(388,72,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(389,72,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-72\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(390,75,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/artist-naqsh.jpg'),(391,75,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:567;s:6:\"height\";i:800;s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"2026/08/artist-naqsh.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:123691;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"artist-naqsh-213x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:213;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:18832;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:24:\"artist-naqsh-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8537;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(392,74,'_thumbnail_id','197'),(393,74,'portrait','197'),(394,74,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(395,74,'origin','Raj has won numerous awards for her painting, including the 2024 ‘Nigaah Award’, presented at Mohatta Palace, Karachi. In 2023, she was shortlisted for the prestigious ‘John Moores Painting Prize’ and received the main prize in ‘Open 23’ at Tarpey Gallery, UK. Her work is exhibited and collected internationally.'),(396,74,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(397,74,'intro','Raj has won numerous awards for her painting, including the 2024 ‘Nigaah Award’, presented at Mohatta Palace, Karachi. In 2023, she was shortlisted for the prestigious ‘John Moores Painting Prize’ and received the main prize in ‘Open 23’ at Tarpey Gallery, UK. Her work is exhibited and collected internationally.'),(398,74,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(399,74,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25631\" class=\"elementor elementor-25631\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Naqsh Raj (b.1984) is an artist, educator and a mother. Until December 2023, Raj was teaching at the Art &amp; Design department at Nottingham Trent International College, UK. She has a Masters Degree in Visual Arts from the National College of Arts, Lahore. She served in Pakistan as an Art educator for ten years at Comsats University, Islamabad. Raj has won numerous awards for her painting, including the 2024 ‘Nigaah Award’, presented at Mohatta Palace, Karachi. In 2023, she was shortlisted for the prestigious ‘John Moores Painting Prize’ and received the main prize in ‘Open 23’ at Tarpey Gallery, UK. Her work is exhibited and collected internationally.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-176ef4b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"176ef4b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				EDUCATION				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c7eab8a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c7eab8a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Master of VIsual Art, National College of Arts, Lahore</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4ce00ca elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4ce00ca\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				SOLO EXHIBITIONS				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ad00514 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ad00514\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>2024 Klangfarben, Galerie Klaus Braun – Stuttgart, Germany.<br />2023 Escape with the Homeland, Galerie Klaus Braun, Stuttgart, Germany.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b6af060 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b6af060\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				SELECTED GROUP EXHIBITIONS				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a465da0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"a465da0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>2024 Summer Salon” Mura Ma Art Space, Manchester, UK.<br />2024 “Holding Up” (three person show), Mura Ma Art Space, Manchester, UK</p><p>2024 “That… Which Binds Us” A Collateral Event to Lahore Biennale 03, Ejaz Gallery, Lahore.<br />2024 “ Next Nature” Three person show, TANZARA Gallery, Islamabad.<br />2024 National Women Exhibition “HERSTORY”, Pakistan National Council of<br />Arts. Islamabad.2023 OPEN, Tarpey Gallery, UK.<br />2022 “LIMINAL”, HAAM Gallery, Lahore.<br />2022 “The Winners “, Gallery 6, Islamabad.<br />2022 Anna Molka Award Exhibition, Punjab University, Lahore.<br />2022 Art Exhibition on Kashmir Solidarity Day, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Islamabad.</p><p>2022 Inaugural exhibition of Islamabad art Gallery F9, Islamabad.</p><p>2021 Alhamra 3rd National Exhibition of Visual Arts, Lahore.</p><p>2020 Onrushing-4, Gallery 6, Islamabad.</p><p>2017 9th National Exhibition, Pakistan National Council of Arts, Islamabad.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b3ff588 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b3ff588\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Press				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-90eaebc elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"90eaebc\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>https://www.monopol-magazin.de/shows/naqsh-raj-escape-homeland<br />https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ziBytitPH0<br />https://tribune.com.pk/story/2486095/next-nature-exhibit-attracts-art-enthusiasts<br />https://www.dawn.com/news/1856082</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6c9ef90 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6c9ef90\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				memberships				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b9d075 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"9b9d075\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Primary, an artist-led contemporary visual arts organisation based in the UK.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-fa4ba4b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"fa4ba4b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				TEACHING AND LECTURING				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-93dc69b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"93dc69b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Visiting Lecturer : Nottingham Trent International College of Art and Design , 2022 – 2023<br />Assistant Professor : COMSATS University – Islamabad, 2014 – 2021</p><p>2024 Nigaah Award, Mohatta Palace Karachi.<br />2023 Main Prize Winner, Open 23, Tarpey Gallery, UK.<br />2023 John Moores Painting Prize (short Listed).<br />2017 Arjumand Painting Award.<br />2009 “ REFRESHED “ Young Artist Exhibition Award, Alhamra Art Council, Lahore.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4b6a7e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"e4b6a7e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				ARTIST RESIDENCY				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-331ac09 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"331ac09\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Vasl-Rohtas International Residency, Islamabad, 2011</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a2f2e34 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a2f2e34\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIBLIOGRAPHY				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7324321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"7324321\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p><a href=\"https://nancollantine.substack.com/p/an-interview-with-artist-naqsh-raj\">https://nancollantine.substack.com/p/an-interview-with-artist-naqsh-raj</a></p><p><a href=\"https://promenadesduregard.blogspot.com/2024/09/naqsh-raj-lart-de-l-impossible.html\">https://promenadesduregard.blogspot.com/2024/09/naqsh-raj-lart-de-l-impossible.html</a></p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(400,74,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(401,74,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(402,74,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(403,74,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(404,74,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-74\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(405,76,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/oblivion.webp'),(406,76,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:723;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"2026/08/oblivion.webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:61820;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"oblivion-212x300.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:212;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:12566;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"oblivion-150x150.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5672;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(407,27,'_thumbnail_id','136'),(408,27,'hero_image','136'),(409,27,'_hero_image','field_xva_exhibition_hero'),(410,78,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/ex-after-image.jpg'),(411,78,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1587;s:6:\"height\";i:2245;s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"2026/08/ex-after-image.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:557240;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"ex-after-image-212x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:212;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:25047;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"ex-after-image-724x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:724;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:168034;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:26:\"ex-after-image-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10344;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"ex-after-image-768x1086.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1086;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:184070;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"ex-after-image-1086x1536.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1086;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:309855;}s:9:\"2048x2048\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"ex-after-image-1448x2048.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1448;s:6:\"height\";i:2048;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:471804;}s:8:\"xva-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"ex-after-image-1587x1500.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1587;s:6:\"height\";i:1500;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:395118;}s:12:\"xva-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"ex-after-image-1000x1250.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1000;s:6:\"height\";i:1250;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:241367;}s:8:\"xva-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:27:\"ex-after-image-900x1125.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1125;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:205055;}s:8:\"xva-wide\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"ex-after-image-1587x1100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1587;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:284642;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(413,77,'hero_image','138'),(414,77,'_hero_image','field_xva_exhibition_hero'),(415,77,'subtitle','XVA Gallery / Exhibition'),(416,77,'_subtitle','field_xva_exhibition_subtitle'),(417,77,'start_date','20260618'),(418,77,'_start_date','field_xva_exhibition_start_date'),(419,77,'end_date','20260716'),(420,77,'_end_date','field_xva_exhibition_end_date'),(421,77,'status_label','past'),(422,77,'_status_label','field_xva_exhibition_status'),(423,77,'intro','Join us from 18 June to 16 July 2026 for Charlie Koolhaas&#8217; After the Image'),(424,77,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(425,77,'venue','XVA Gallery'),(426,77,'_venue','field_xva_exhibition_venue'),(427,77,'curatorial_text','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"26455\" class=\"elementor elementor-26455\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9c0535e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9c0535e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2bc27a2 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2bc27a2\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>At XVA Art Hotel, Charlie Koolhaas presents After the Image, a project that turns one of the hotel rooms into a lived-in archive of Dubai’s architectural past.</p><p>Moving between a hotel room installation and a gallery presentation, the exhibition brings together photography, textiles, sculpture, and everyday objects drawn from Koolhaas’ long-term research into the city’s changing urban landscape.</p><p>Charlie&#8217;s photographs record Dubai&#8217;s architectural history through the details that are often passed over: facades, tiles, patterns, textures and surfaces. She then transforms these images into sculpture, clothing, furniture and objects, bringing fragments of the city&#8217;s modern heritage into the room, the hand and onto the body, giving them another life beyond the photograph.</p><p>XVA Art Hotel has its own place in this history. As one of Dubai’s early contemporary art spaces, set within the heritage architecture of Al Fahidi, it sits between preservation and experiment, between the old city and the cultural scene that grew around it.</p><p>In After the Image, the room itself becomes the archive. Rather than treating the archive as something sealed away, the project makes it porous, domestic, and alive.</p><p><em>This project is supported through the Modern Heritage Grant Program, an initiative by the UAE Ministry of Culture, in collaboration with Zayed University and Majra – National CSR Fund.</em></p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-83ab635 elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\" data-id=\"83ab635\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"button.default\">\n										<a class=\"elementor-button elementor-button-link elementor-size-sm\" href=\"http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/After-the-Image-Press-Release-.pdf.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n						<span class=\"elementor-button-content-wrapper\">\n									<span class=\"elementor-button-text\">View Press Release</span>\n					</span>\n					</a>\n								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-863a80f elementor-hidden-desktop elementor-hidden-tablet elementor-hidden-mobile_extra elementor-hidden-mobile elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"863a80f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Bio</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-eda4a53 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-hidden-desktop elementor-hidden-tablet elementor-hidden-mobile_extra elementor-hidden-mobile elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"eda4a53\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in Edinburgh in 1976 and raised in Hong Kong, Jane Bailey Beveridge is a visual artist and dedicated art educator based in Dubai. She studied Graphic Design and Fine Art at the University of Brighton, graduating in 1998. In 2002, she joined the Art Department at Dubai College, where she has served as Head of Art since 2007.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(428,77,'_curatorial_text','field_xva_exhibition_curatorial_text'),(429,77,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(430,77,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-77\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"exhibition\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(431,80,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/ex-local.jpeg'),(432,80,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:949;s:6:\"height\";i:1658;s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"2026/08/ex-local.jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:1558064;s:5:\"sizes\";a:9:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"ex-local-172x300.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:172;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:9588;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-586x1024.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:586;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:102166;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:21:\"ex-local-150x150.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5286;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-768x1342.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:1342;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:182909;}s:9:\"1536x1536\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-879x1536.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:879;s:6:\"height\";i:1536;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:245793;}s:8:\"xva-hero\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-949x1500.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:949;s:6:\"height\";i:1500;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:351143;}s:12:\"xva-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-949x1250.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:949;s:6:\"height\";i:1250;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:301128;}s:8:\"xva-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-900x1125.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:1125;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:197403;}s:8:\"xva-wide\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"ex-local-949x1100.jpeg\";s:5:\"width\";i:949;s:6:\"height\";i:1100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:264989;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:10:\"1778767634\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(433,79,'_thumbnail_id','140'),(434,79,'hero_image','140'),(435,79,'_hero_image','field_xva_exhibition_hero'),(436,79,'subtitle','XVA Gallery / Exhibition'),(437,79,'_subtitle','field_xva_exhibition_subtitle'),(438,79,'start_date',''),(439,79,'_start_date','field_xva_exhibition_start_date'),(440,79,'end_date',''),(441,79,'_end_date','field_xva_exhibition_end_date'),(442,79,'status_label','past'),(443,79,'_status_label','field_xva_exhibition_status'),(444,79,'intro','Join us from May 23rd to June 18th 2026 for Jane Beveridge&#8217;s first solo show that captures the essence of Dubai, and belonging.'),(445,79,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(446,79,'venue','XVA Gallery'),(447,79,'_venue','field_xva_exhibition_venue'),(448,79,'curatorial_text','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"26432\" class=\"elementor elementor-26432\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9c0535e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9c0535e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f3e04b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6f3e04b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Artist Statement</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8a02e3a elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8a02e3a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Swimming pools and construction sites. Dusty DIY stores and haberdasheries. The kind that have been there forever &#8211; or at least since 2002, when I arrived in Dubai. Jam-packed from floor to ceiling with thread, fabric, tools, and brightly coloured domestic objects, these spaces are crammed with possibility. They are often overlooked in a city best known for its malls and extravagance, but they are among my most cherished places in Dubai.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9eed6cf elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"9eed6cf\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>DUBAI is a five letter word, as is LOCAL. For years, I have been collecting five-letter words &#8211; from TRUST to TRUTH, VOICE to GRACE, ALIVE to TOUCH. Five is the limit of complexity for the human mind, according to mathematician Frank Ramsey. Beyond that number the thresholds for order grow at an extraordinary rate &#8211; faster than exponentials, faster than anything we can compute. My background in Graphic Design, studied in the 1990s, instilled in me a lasting fascination with the form and meaning of letters, numbers, and words; the emotional power of language intertwined with the visual power of art.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a46e436 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"a46e436\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Beyond this, my visual palette and material inspiration are rooted in the streets. I am drawn to the beauty of cracked, stained, and weathered walls as well as surfaces patched with plaster or paint &#8211; they read like large abstract paintings. Corrugated cardboard, concrete, sand, rust, tangled wires, weathered wood &#8211; all find their way into my work, each carrying a story of time, place and texture.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2bc27a2 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2bc27a2\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>I am captivated by the ordered mosaics that line swimming pools. Much like swimming lengths of a pool, repetition is central to my practice. The rhythmic act of gluing tiles or stitching, wrapping, knotting &#8211; repeating the same gesture over and over &#8211; becomes meditative, a quiet form of devotion. Whether working with paint, string, fabric or mosaic, I am fascinated by pattern, rhythm, and the quiet persistence of making.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-863a80f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"863a80f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Bio</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-eda4a53 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"eda4a53\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in Edinburgh in 1976 and raised in Hong Kong, Jane Bailey Beveridge is a visual artist and dedicated art educator based in Dubai. She studied Graphic Design and Fine Art at the University of Brighton, graduating in 1998. In 2002, she joined the Art Department at Dubai College, where she has served as Head of Art since 2007.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-0052e3d elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"0052e3d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Her work is informed by a background in Asian contemporary culture and graphic design, which fostered a lasting fascination with the form, symbolism, and emotional resonance of language. This interest is further shaped by the urban landscape of Dubai, particularly its ever-present construction sites. Drawing on these influences, Beveridge creates mixed-media assemblages that combine painting with mosaic, textiles, found objects, and concrete. She often refers to these works as “five-letter-word adverts”, exploring the intersection of language, materiality, and visual impact.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(449,79,'_curatorial_text','field_xva_exhibition_curatorial_text'),(450,79,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(451,79,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-source-79\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"exhibition\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(452,82,'_wp_attached_file','2026/08/ex-white.jpg'),(453,82,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:722;s:6:\"height\";i:1087;s:4:\"file\";s:20:\"2026/08/ex-white.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:70476;s:5:\"sizes\";a:3:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:20:\"ex-white-199x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:199;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5564;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s