Contemporary Art, Boulder, CO, A Sense of Place, exhibition catalogue, 2004<br />Pratt Institute, Brooklyn, NY, Juried Alumni Exhibition, exhibition catalogue, 2002<br />University of Stockholm, Stockholm, Sweden, 12th International Conference of IWSF, exhibition catalogue, 2001<br />University of California at Berkeley, Berkeley, CA, Beyond Boundaries, exhibition catalogue, 2000<br />Art Museum of South Texas, Corpus Christi, TX, Artcapades, exhibition catalogue, 2000</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b40a379 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"b40a379\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-bd7a81a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"bd7a81a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bibliography				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-62dc56d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"62dc56d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Legrand, Amandine, Exposition Graines Sacrées – Institut des Cultures d’Islam, www.artistikrezo.com, October 28, 2016<br />Tisseyre, Sarah, «Sacrées Graines», quand le couscous pose des question, www.rfi.fr, October 17, 2016<br />Doucouré, Samba and Huê Trinh Nguyên, « Sacrées graines » : le couscous fait roi, www.saphirnews.com, September 7, 2016<br />Canestrier, Edith, « Sacrées Graines », edithcanestrier.wordpress.com, September, 2016<br />Sorgatz, Mike, “The Retrieval of the Beautiful , www.artinnewyorkcity.com, June 21, 2016<br />Ali, M, ‘Shifting’ by Banu Colak &amp; Naz Shahrokh, www.dubainewspost.com, May 3, 2016<br />Dahlawia, Fazial, Shifting, a new art exhibition reinterpreting our world-All about interconnectedness, www.buro247.me, May 3, 2016<br />Egerton, Laura, “Raw Materials: Crafting as Fine Art”, Vision Magazine, September 2015<br />Dessurne, Elisha, “Maintaining the present: A Connective Effort in Dubai”, Ziwira, September 4, 2015<br />Silveira, Danilo, “Substainable Art”, Medalhao Persa, Summer 2015, p.12-15<br />Kalsi, Jyoti, “Expressions of Sustainability”, Gulf News, April 15, 2015<br />Grahm, Anne, “Naz Shahrokh”, Art Reveal Magazine, Issue 3, April 2015, p.46-51<br />Frey, Andrew, “New Artist Feature Fall2014”, CultureHall, Feature Issue 113, October 8-November 4, 2014<br />Rutigliano, Dario,”Naz Shahrokh: Interview”, LandEscape Art Press, November 2014 Special Issue, p.20-35<br />Pirillo, Francesca, “Naz Shahrokh: Interview”, Made In Mind Magazine, Issue 01, Spring 2014, p.3-12<br />McEneaney, Caroline, “Let’s get this Show on the Road”. Time Out Abu Dhabi, February 2014, Vol. 13, Issue 5, p.18<br />Kazan, Sophie, “The Conceptual Artist Naz Shahrokh – The Nature of Art “, Islamic ArtsMagazine.com, 2012<br />Parker, Sharon, “Naz Shahrokh: Remembering, Recycling and Roots”, Contemporary Practices, March 2011, vol. 8, p.204<br />Etherington, Victoria, “A Fresh Perspective”, Gulf News Magazine, June 2010, p.39<br />Mehassien, Enas, “Insurgency Draws Beauty in Abu Dhabi “, Emarat Alyoum, April 28, 2010, p.24<br />Kassed, Salman, “59 Artworks Exhibition in Abu Dhabi “, Al Ittihad, April 27, 2010, p.21<br />Younes, Abeer, “Raw Materials and a Variety of Decorative Art in the Exhibition”, Al Bayan, April 27, 2010, p.38<br />Wilks, Jon, “Journey’s End”, Time Out Abu Dhabi, April 2010, Vol. 9, Issue 4, p.44<br />Seaman, Anna, “Graffiti Helps University Students link Islam with Art”, The National, October 28, 2009, Volume 2, Issue 195, p.8<br />Genocchio, Benjamin, “A Chance to Fill Up on Visual Treats”, New York Times, April 25, 2004, Section 14, p.93<br />Boros, Phyllis A.S. “Silvermine Showcases Some of the Regions Finest Artworks”, Connecticut Post, May 11, 2003, p.E1<br />Eliasoph, Philip, “Getting an Eyeful at Silvermine”, Connecticut Post, May 25, 2003, p.G1<br />Streitfeld, L.P., “54th Art of the Northeast”, The Advocate &amp; Greenwich Time, May 18, 2003, p.D3<br />Golonu, Berin, “Beyond Boundaries”, ART PAPERS, November/December, 2000, p.52<br />Lvof, Nan, “72 artists focus on ‘1x1x1: Visions of the Millennium”, Greenwich Time, December 6, 1999, p.A8</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1242,185,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1243,185,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1244,185,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1245,185,'origin','Bio Born in Tehran, Iran 1969; Lives and works in Abu Dhabi, UAE Naz Shahrokh is a visual artist who lives and works in Abu Dhabi, UAE. Her current work involves photography, drawing, video, and installation, and throughout her studio practice, Naz strives to find a connection that is significant in conjunction to society, the [&hellip;]'),(1246,185,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1247,185,'artwork_gallery','a:11:{i:0;i:187;i:1;i:722;i:2;i:723;i:3;i:724;i:4;i:725;i:5;i:726;i:6;i:727;i:7;i:728;i:8;i:729;i:9;i:730;i:10;i:731;}'),(1248,185,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1249,190,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/artist/nasr-warour/'),(1250,190,'_xva_source_id','25649'),(1251,190,'_xva_source_content','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25649\" class=\"elementor elementor-25649\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				About the Artist				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Born in 1968 in Syria, Nasr Warour holds a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree from Damascus University; he also studied at the fine art institute in Swaida, Syria. Nasr’s interests comprise art, sculpture and literature. He started with sculpture before dedicating himself to painting. This talented artist also writes poetry in Arabic and often weaves it into his works.</p><p>He has been participating to art shows since 1986. Nasr’s work has been exhibited in forums and galleries in Syria and abroad, notably in Dubai, Lebanon and New Delhi. He participated recently to several joint exhibitions in Dubai and Bahrain. In 2009, he won the fourth award of Lorenzo il Magnifico in the Seventh Edition of Florence Biennale of Contemporary Art 2009.<br />Since 2000, the artist lives and works in Dubai.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1252,190,'_xva_source_modified','2026-06-10T16:08:08'),(1253,192,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm.png'),(1254,192,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:845;s:6:\"height\";i:1058;s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"2025/12/NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm.png\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:1190425;s:5:\"sizes\";a:4:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm-240x300.png\";s:5:\"width\";i:240;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:9:\"image/png\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:66103;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:71:\"NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm-818x1024.png\";s:5:\"width\";i:818;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:9:\"image/png\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:799872;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm-150x150.png\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:9:\"image/png\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:21053;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"NW32-image-COVER-PHOUntitled-Coral-and-wood-45-x-18-x-7-cm-768x962.png\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:962;s:9:\