hat permeates our spirit into serenity and balance.”The Oneness Of Being,Katia Al [&hellip;]'),(1453,226,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(1454,226,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25520\" class=\"elementor elementor-25520\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1970 Amman, Jordan</p><p>“When in the presence of ancient knowledge and at your most raw, fluidity is achieved. Our outer layers are shed and we are only left with the truth of our existence. We are transcendent beauty and elegance that permeates our spirit into serenity and balance.”<br />The Oneness Of Being,<br />Katia Al Tal<br />A sculptor at heart, it came naturally to Al Tal to work with clay and produce Nuwa Creations ceramics; a series of practical everyday objects that are pure of colour and line; delicate but sturdy and completely sculptural.</p><p>Al Tal’s work is a mixture of art and aesthetic that is multi functional, decorative and, above all, creative, resulting is great appreciation from a wide range of consumers.</p><p>Her creations are found in both private collections, as well as Museums and art galleries. Due to their functionality as household pieces these works of art are capable of pleasing the most exigent art critic.</p><p>Al Tal’s creations are a culmination of her authentic, mystical and spiritual inner world along with her internal experiences that are brought to life through her skills in various art mediums starting with theater, film making, sculpting and ceramics .<br />Her journey into sculpture, calligraphy and ceramics was a natural continuity and a fluid part of her creative trip. It is through ceramics that the ancient soul of clay and calligraphy is revived and allowed to vibrate again with renewed life in a postmodern era.</p><p>Her sculptural work is a striking combination of unusual complexity; perfectly molded into minimalistic organic shapes.<br />Al Tal lives between France and Jordan</p><p><a href=\"https://privateviews.artlogic.net/2/7d846bf1293eda7aee48e3/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Catalog of Available Works »</a></p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1994 Performing Arts Center, City, Amman, Jordan – Certificate in Drama<br />1996 Lyon University, Lyon, France – French Diploma<br />1993 B.A., University of Jordan, Amman, Jordan – Bachelor of Arts: Psychology and Political Science</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2023 Appearance, XVA Gallery, Dubai, UAE<br />2015 Dimension of Civilization, Yinchuan Museum Of Contemporary Art, Yinchuan, China<br />2013 70 years of Contemporary Jordanian Art, Jordan National Gallery of Fine Arts<br />2013 Eva, Jordan National Gallery of Fine Arts<br />2013 VISIBLE DIFFERENCES, Jordan National Gallery of Fine Arts<br />2012 Artist of the month, Jordan National Gallery of Fine Arts<br />2009 Environmental Themes Sculpture Exhibition, Dubai, UAE<br />2008 Asian Contemporary Art Fair, New York, USA<br />2008 Clay Sculpture Exhibition, Muscat, Oman<br />2007 “Dar Al Ataa” Fundraiser Exhibition, Muscat, Oman<br />2006 Clay Figurine Sculpture Exhibition, Amman, Jordan<br />2006 “Doctors without Borders” Fundraiser Art Exhibition, Dubai, UAE<br />2004 Sculpture Exhibition at XVA Gallery, Dubai, UAE</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1455,226,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1456,226,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1457,226,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1458,226,'origin','Bio Born in 1970 Amman, Jordan “When in the presence of ancient knowledge and at your most raw, fluidity is achieved. Our outer layers are shed and we are only left with the truth of our existence. We are transcendent beauty and elegance that permeates our spirit into serenity and balance.”The Oneness Of Being,Katia Al [&hellip;]'),(1459,226,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1460,226,'artwork_gallery','a:13:{i:0;i:229;i:1;i:809;i:2;i:810;i:3;i:811;i:4;i:812;i:5;i:813;i:6;i:814;i:7;i:815;i:8;i:816;i:9;i:817;i:10;i:818;i:11;i:819;i:12;i:820;}'),(1461,226,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1462,229,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1.jpg'),(1463,229,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1320;s:6:\"height\";i:882;s:4:\"file\";s:85:\"2025/12/KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:128099;s:5:\"sizes\";a:6:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:85:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:7721;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:86:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-1024x684.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:684;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:62748;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:85:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:4177;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:85:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-768x513.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:513;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:36062;}s:12:\"xva-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:86:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-1000x882.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1000;s:6:\"height\";i:882;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:96790;}s:8:\"xva-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:85:\"KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair-1-900x882.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:882;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:81557;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(1464,229,'_xva_source_media_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/KATD-009-imageAzraq-Tea-Cup-and-Saucer-2013-Ceramic-stone-wear-Per-Pair.jpg'),(1465,229,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Katia Al Tal'),(1466,230,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/artist/jonathan-gent/'),(1467,230,'_xva_source_id','25511'),(1468,230,'_xva_source_content','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25511\" class=\"elementor elementor-25511\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Jonathan Gent was born in 1976. After studying at The Cheshire School of Art and The Edinburgh School of Art respectively, he then worked and lived between France and Los Angeles. He has recently moved from California to The Highlands in Scotland. Gent’s paintings have been exhibited widely throughout the world including Edinburgh’s Scottish national Gallery, The Saatchi Gallery, The Freud Museum, and has recently held solo shows in Dubai, Los Angeles, New York and London. Gent has gained a strong reputation with collectors including Tilda Swinton, Robin Vousden, Rami Farook, Samantha Morton, Aimee Mullins, Simon Hillary, John Papsidera, David and Tia Hoberman.<br />Gent has warranted coverage in magazines such as I-D, W magazine, Another Magazine, Time Out, and Self Service. Gent makes paintings and drawings which present an inventive, gnarled vision of human complication.</p><p>Born in 1976 in Cheshire England</p><p>Lives The Highlands Scotland</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1993-95 Cheshire School of Art – Painting<br />1995-98 Edinburgh school of Art – Drawing &amp; Painting</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – HOTEL “america”<br />London England</p><p>2004 – GLU Gallery “This is the one they’re going to remember me for”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2005 – GLU Gallery “Shapes and Colours”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2008 – XVA “Views Of The Eternal City”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – CARTER PRESENTS “england”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – XVA “Women (Vol.1)”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2012 –Mummery &amp; Schnelle “11 Paintings”<br />London England</p><p>2013- FallonBarr “Amuse Bouche”<br />New York USA</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – The Freud Museum “The royal road to the unconscious”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – ALEF &amp; Phillips de Pury &amp; Co “Regional Delicacies: Alef’s Art Mezze”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – XVA Artist in Residence The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – THE PRINTSPACE “10”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – The Wharf Project “Dystopia For All”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – CARTER PRESENTS “A Shot In The Arm”<br />London England</p><p>2009 – “A Shot In The Dark”<br />Chateau Radvanov<br />Czech Republic</p><p>2009 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – La Lanta Gallery “Another Side”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Leroy House “Mortars At Dawn”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – DOB gallery “On The Edge”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Saatchi Gallery “Art of Giving”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – Traffic “I don’t need Your Money Honey, All I Need is Love – works from The Farook Collection<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2011 – Harris Lindsay “Now and Then” by Adrian Dannatt<br />London England</p><p>2012 – New Museum of Liverpool “Liverpool Love”<br />Liverpool England</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a695bbd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a695bbd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Fairs				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d28e438 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d28e438\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2008 – The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – SCOPE<br />London England</p><p>2009 – BAF<br />Dubai UAE</p></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1469,230,'_xva_source_modified','2025-12-17T12:19:28'),(1470,231,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/JG-31-image-cover-photoOld-Boat-on-Creek-2013-Mixed-media-varnish-on-wood-15-x-20-cm.jpg'),(1471,231,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:577;s:6:\"height\";i:431;s:4:\"file\";s:96:\"2025/12/JG-31-image-cover-photoOld-Boat-on-Creek-2013-Mixed-media-varnish-on-wood-15-x-20-cm.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:20811;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:96:\"JG-31-image-cover-photoOld-Boat-on-Creek-2013-Mixed-media-varnish-on-wood-15-x-20-cm-300x224.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:224;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5512;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:96:\"JG-31-image-cover-photoOld-Boat-on-Creek-2013-Mixed-media-v