>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Jonathan Gent was born in 1976. After studying at The Cheshire School of Art and The Edinburgh School of Art respectively, he then worked and lived between France and Los Angeles. He has recently moved from California to The Highlands in Scotland. Gent’s paintings have been exhibited widely throughout the world including Edinburgh’s Scottish national Gallery, The Saatchi Gallery, The Freud Museum, and has recently held solo shows in Dubai, Los Angeles, New York and London. Gent has gained a strong reputation with collectors including Tilda Swinton, Robin Vousden, Rami Farook, Samantha Morton, Aimee Mullins, Simon Hillary, John Papsidera, David and Tia Hoberman.<br />Gent has warranted coverage in magazines such as I-D, W magazine, Another Magazine, Time Out, and Self Service. Gent makes paintings and drawings which present an inventive, gnarled vision of human complication.</p><p>Born in 1976 in Cheshire England</p><p>Lives The Highlands Scotland</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1993-95 Cheshire School of Art – Painting<br />1995-98 Edinburgh school of Art – Drawing &amp; Painting</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – HOTEL “america”<br />London England</p><p>2004 – GLU Gallery “This is the one they’re going to remember me for”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2005 – GLU Gallery “Shapes and Colours”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2008 – XVA “Views Of The Eternal City”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – CARTER PRESENTS “england”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – XVA “Women (Vol.1)”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2012 –Mummery &amp; Schnelle “11 Paintings”<br />London England</p><p>2013- FallonBarr “Amuse Bouche”<br />New York USA</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – The Freud Museum “The royal road to the unconscious”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – ALEF &amp; Phillips de Pury &amp; Co “Regional Delicacies: Alef’s Art Mezze”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – XVA Artist in Residence The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – THE PRINTSPACE “10”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – The Wharf Project “Dystopia For All”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – CARTER PRESENTS “A Shot In The Arm”<br />London England</p><p>2009 – “A Shot In The Dark”<br />Chateau Radvanov<br />Czech Republic</p><p>2009 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – La Lanta Gallery “Another Side”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Leroy House “Mortars At Dawn”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – DOB gallery “On The Edge”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Saatchi Gallery “Art of Giving”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – Traffic “I don’t need Your Money Honey, All I Need is Love – works from The Farook Collection<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2011 – Harris Lindsay “Now and Then” by Adrian Dannatt<br />London England</p><p>2012 – New Museum of Liverpool “Liverpool Love”<br />Liverpool England</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a695bbd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a695bbd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Fairs				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d28e438 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d28e438\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2008 – The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – SCOPE<br />London England</p><p>2009 – BAF<br />Dubai UAE</p></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1485,230,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25511\" class=\"elementor elementor-25511\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Jonathan Gent was born in 1976. After studying at The Cheshire School of Art and The Edinburgh School of Art respectively, he then worked and lived between France and Los Angeles. He has recently moved from California to The Highlands in Scotland. Gent’s paintings have been exhibited widely throughout the world including Edinburgh’s Scottish national Gallery, The Saatchi Gallery, The Freud Museum, and has recently held solo shows in Dubai, Los Angeles, New York and London. Gent has gained a strong reputation with collectors including Tilda Swinton, Robin Vousden, Rami Farook, Samantha Morton, Aimee Mullins, Simon Hillary, John Papsidera, David and Tia Hoberman.<br />Gent has warranted coverage in magazines such as I-D, W magazine, Another Magazine, Time Out, and Self Service. Gent makes paintings and drawings which present an inventive, gnarled vision of human complication.</p><p>Born in 1976 in Cheshire England</p><p>Lives The Highlands Scotland</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1993-95 Cheshire School of Art – Painting<br />1995-98 Edinburgh school of Art – Drawing &amp; Painting</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – HOTEL “america”<br />London England</p><p>2004 – GLU Gallery “This is the one they’re going to remember me for”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2005 – GLU Gallery “Shapes and Colours”<br />Los Angeles USA</p><p>2008 – XVA “Views Of The Eternal City”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – CARTER PRESENTS “england”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – XVA “Women (Vol.1)”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2012 –Mummery &amp; Schnelle “11 Paintings”<br />London England</p><p>2013- FallonBarr “Amuse Bouche”<br />New York USA</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2004 – The Freud Museum “The royal road to the unconscious”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – ALEF &amp; Phillips de Pury &amp; Co “Regional Delicacies: Alef’s Art Mezze”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – XVA Artist in Residence The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – THE PRINTSPACE “10”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – The Wharf Project “Dystopia For All”<br />London England</p><p>2008 – CARTER PRESENTS “A Shot In The Arm”<br />London England</p><p>2009 – “A Shot In The Dark”<br />Chateau Radvanov<br />Czech Republic</p><p>2009 – XVA “summer collection”<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2010 – La Lanta Gallery “Another Side”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Leroy House “Mortars At Dawn”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – DOB gallery “On The Edge”<br />Bangkok Thailand</p><p>2010 – Saatchi Gallery “Art of Giving”<br />London England</p><p>2010 – Traffic “I don’t need Your Money Honey, All I Need is Love – works from The Farook Collection<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2011 – Harris Lindsay “Now and Then” by Adrian Dannatt<br />London England</p><p>2012 – New Museum of Liverpool “Liverpool Love”<br />Liverpool England</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a695bbd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a695bbd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Fairs				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d28e438 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d28e438\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2008 – The Creek Art Fair<br />Dubai UAE</p><p>2008 – SCOPE<br />London England</p><p>2009 – BAF<br />Dubai UAE</p></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1486,230,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1487,230,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1488,230,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1489,230,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1490,230,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1491,230,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1492,230,'origin','Bio Jonathan Gent was born in 1976. After studying at The Cheshire School of Art and The Edinburgh School of Art respectively, he then worked and lived between France and Los Angeles. He has recently moved from California to The Highlands in Scotland. Gent’s paintings have been exhibited widely throughout the world including Edinburgh’s Scottish [&hellip;]'),(1493,230,'origin','Bio Jonathan Gent was born in 1976. After studying at The Cheshire School of Art and The Edinburgh School of Art respectively, he then worked and lived between France and Los Angeles. He has recently moved from California to The Highlands in Scotland. Gent’s paintings have been exhibited widely throughout the world including Edinburgh’s Scottish [&hellip;]'),(1494,230,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1495,230,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1496,230,'artwork_gallery','a:4:{i:0;i:231;i:1;i:821;i:2;i:822;i:3;i:823;}'),(1497,230,'artwork_gallery','a:4:{i:0;i:231;i:1;i:821;i:2;i:822;i:3;i:823;}'),(1498,230,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1499,230,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1500,233,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/artist/jakob-roepke/'),(1501,233,'_xva_source_id','25484'),(1502,233,'_xva_source_content','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25484\" class=\"elementor elementor-25484\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore</p><p>Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, installation and digital technology as means to re-examine historical documents and their influence, so inviting audiences to contemplate the contradictions of how we record and understand history.</p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2008 MA (Hons.) Visual Arts, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2004 BFA, National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: “Lost Pages From One Thousand and One Nights, Canvas Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2019: “Dust to Dust” at Kang Contemporary Gallery, Berlin, DE.<br />2018: “Pasts in Particles ” at Twelve Twelve Gallery, Den Haag, NL.<br />2018: “Holy Water” Open Studio 2018, at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2017: “Light on the Fringe of Time” Open Studio at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2015: “Enclosure/Erasure”, solo show at Koel Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2013 Art Basel Hong Kong, Hong Kong<br />2012 Lik Likoti, Canvas Gallery, Karachi<br />2011 The Memory is the Message, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Twelve Gates Art Gallery, Philadelphia<br />2010 Badshahnama, Solo show at Tmproject Gallery Geneva</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2019: “Neighbourhoods and Communities” Sommerfest, at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2019: “Engaging with Histories” at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2019: “Badshahnama” 2 Person Show at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE.<br />2019: “Mera Safar” Koel Galleery Karachi, PK.<br />2018: “within /without ” Asia House London.UK.<br />2018: “Seen Unseen” Kasteel Oud-Rekem, BE.<br />2018: “Revelation: Reclaiming South Asian Narratives” exhibition and seminar at Harvard university, South Asia Institute, Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA.<br />2018: “Changing Places” Phoenix, Leicester, UK.<br />2017: “The Materiality of the Invisible” at Marres, Centre for Contemporary Culture Maastricht, NL.<br />2017: “The Great Wall” Karachi Biennale, PK.<br />2017: “Changing Places” Hastings Museum &amp; Art Gallery, UK.<br />2017: “Taqseem” koel gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2016: “The Materiality of the Invisible #01” at Jan Van Eyck Academie, Maastricht, NL.<br />2016: “Hopes of Paradise ”, at Grosvenor gallery London. UK.<br />2016: “Vanishing Point” Artport, Tel Aviv, IL.<br />2016: “IFAA Contemporary Project Phase I” at Solutions! Musee de L’Art et de I’Espace, Paris, FR.<br />2015: “The Lay of the Land”, at Gallery Latitude 28, New Delhi IND.<br />2015: “Art15 London”, with Khaas Gallery, UK.<br />2014: “SINDH Reverberating sounds echo through the dessert” at Koel Gallery, Karachi, PK.<br />2014: “I.D” at the Islamabad Literature Festival 2014 by MyArtWorld gallery, Islamabad, PK.<br />2014: “Stet”, at LLF, Alhamra art Gallery, Lahore, PK.<br />2013 27th Annual Exhibition of Punjab Art Association, Alhamra Arts Council, Lahore<br />2013 Paper, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2012 Faculty Show at Zahoor-ul-Akhlaq Gallery, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2012 Soul Searchers, 3 person show at Rohtas Gallery, Islamabad<br />2012 Band Baaja Baraat, IVS Gallery, Karachi<br />2011 The Return, 2nd International Festival of Contemporary Art, Museum of Modern &amp; Contemporary Art (MOMA), Algiers<br />2011 After All (curated by Quddus Mirza), Royat Gallery, Lahore<br />2011 Common Threads: Contemporary Art from Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Iran and Pakistan, Xerxes Gallery with NMart gallery at the Bastakiya at the Heritage House Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Finalist Exhibition of the Sovereign Asian Art Prize, The Rotunda, Hong Kong<br />2010 Contemporary Shahnama, millennium painting Exhibition, The Prince’s Foundation Gallery, London<br />2010 The Sovereign Asian Art Prize finalist exhibition, ARTSPACE, Helutrans, Singapore<br />2010 Creating Common Wealth, curated by Ragini Gallery, New Delhi, India<br />2010 Fatah Je Asay Pasay, Green Cardamom at V.M Art Gallery, Karachi &amp; Sindh Museum, Hyderabad<br />2010 Structures Within An Intervention, The Guild Art Gallery, New York<br />2010 Making of The History, Two person show, Canvas Gallery, Karachi<br />2010 The Havelian Express, CAIS Gallery, Hong Kong<br />2009 Tradition &amp; Tension, Art Scene Gallery, Karachi<br />2009 Redo Pakistan, a traveling show, Karachi, Lahore, Pakistan, England, UK, Dhaka, Bangladesh<br />2009 Starring: The Artist, Indus Valley Gallery, Karachi<br />2008 Degree show, Zahoor-ul-Akhalq Gallery, National college of Arts, Lahore<br />2008 Young Artist Exhibition, Alhmara Art Council, Lahore<br />2007 Dropping Tears Together, anokha laadla collective performance, Alhamra Art Council, Lahore<br />2006 Places Real and Imagined, Alhamra Art Gallery, Lahore<br />2005 Voices, Pakistan Development Forum, Islamabad</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a695bbd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a695bbd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Teaching Experience				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d28e438 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d28e438\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: Guest Teacher at Kinnard College for Women, Lahore. PK.<br />2021: Guest Teacher at Institute of Art and Design, University of Sindh, Jamshoro, PK.<br />2017: Guest Teacher at HKU – Beeldende Kunst, Utrecht, NL.<br />2007-2016: Assistant Professor in Department of Fine Arts at National College of Arts, Lahore, PK.<br />2915-16: External examiner for final year at Kinnard College for Women in Lahore, PK.<br />2015: Guest Teacher at Institute of Art &amp; design, Jamshoro, Sindh, PK.<br />2015: External examiner for final year at Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh, PK.<br />2012 : Guest Teacher Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh PK<br />2009 Workshop at Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh<br />2007-present National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-73afb86 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"73afb86\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Articles & Reviews				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-cb53373 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"cb53373\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Quddus Mirza, “ Back to Baghdad” The News newspaper, Pakistan, 24th October, 2021.<br />Numair A. Abbasi, “ The memory of objects” Daily Dawn newpaper, Pakistan. 7th November, 2021.<br />Salman Peerzada, “Lost and Found” Daily Dawn newpaper, Pakistan, 19th October, 2021.<br />Zahid Chaudhary, Itinerant Photography: Medium and Translation in the work of Imran Channa. “Photography in India: From Archives to Contemporary Practice” Published by Bloomsbury, USA.<br />“Dust to Dust” http://www.fvu.co.uk/projects/dust-to-dust<br />Ella Bjurman, About the Issue, Sindh Guardian, https://issuu.com/sapac/docs/sindh_guardian_<br />Iftikhar Dadi, Spectral Memories, Tanqeed, Magazine of art and culture. http://www.tanqeed.org/2016/03/enclosure- erasure-imran-channa/<br />Zarmeene’ Shah, The Hidden Truth, Herald, May 2015, Pakistan.<br />Iftikhar Dadi, Spectral Memories, Enclosure/Erasure exhibition catalogue. Lahore<br />Quddus Mirza, The art of disappearance, Encoure, The News, April 5, 2015. Pakistan.<br />Rabeya Jalil, Reviews: Reworking Memories and Histories, ArtNow Pakistan.<br />Sadia Salim, A journey into abstraction, Daily Dawn, Sunday, April 5, 2015, Pakistan.<br />Interview: Re-aligning historical perspective: in conversation with Amra Ali. Dawn, August 11, 2013.<br />Alina Husain, “Art as communication” Herald, February 2013,Karachi.<br />M. Saeed Qureshi, Elucidating illusion. Daily Dawn, January 19 , 2013, Karachi.<br />Peerzada Salman, Lik Likoti opens at Canvas, 19 Dec , 2012, Daily Dawn, Karachi.<br />Shahim AKhtar, Imran Channa, Lik LIkoti” Pakistan art Review, Karachi.<br />“The Memory is the Message” Al Itihad, Saturday , 11th June, UAE.<br />Meilz Manfred ed, Painting The Persian Book of Kings Today. Cambridge: Talking Tree Books.<br />Ansari, Saira. Three Blind Mice, Papercuts Vol 7. online magazine.<br />Khan Naiza h. 2010. The Rising Tide, The Rising Tide New Directions in art from Pakistan 1990-2010:Karachi, Mohatta Palace Museum.<br />Nasar Hammad. 2010. Engaging Urban Realities Through A ‘Thinking’ Photography. TheRisingTide New Directions in art from Pakistan 1990- 2010:Karachi, Mohatta Palace Museum.<br />Imran Khan!.2010. Myth and reality. Pakistan’s rising tide. AlJazeera. 2010.<br />Asim Akhtar. PAUSE PLAY. Libas international Magazine, Volume 23 issue 22010. Lahore.<br />Quddus Mirza. His pupil’s voice, The News. Jul 2010<br />Nasar Hammad. Fatah jay Aassay Paassay. In the Milieu of fatah Halepoto, published by Green Cardamom, London.<br />Adamjee, Maheen Bashir. Messages for the Discerning, NEWSLINE, 31 May, 2010, Karachi.<br />Ahmad H, Ameer. Nostalgia, experimentalism and political games: ‘Making of History/Green Patrol’. Daily Times, April 15, 2010, Karachi.<br />Yee-Wan Koon, Blindness and Insight, MUSE , February, 2010, Hong Kong.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-552072e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"552072e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Awards, Residencies & Fellowships				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c6b5a50 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c6b5a50\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021-22: Artist in Residence at EYE Filmmuseum, Amsterdam, NL.<br />2019-2020: Artist Fellowship at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2018: Artist Fellowship at Harvard University South Asia Institute, Massachusetts, Boston, USA.<br />2018-21: Recipient of “Werkbijdrage Bewezen Talent” by Mondriaan Fonds. Amsterdam, NL.<br />2013 Award of Excellence, AAP Lahore<br />2011 Gasworks International Residency Programme, London<br />2010 Finalist for the Sovereign Asian Art Prize 2010, Hong Kong<br />2004 Merit scholarship, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2003 Merit scholarship, National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1503,233,'_xva_source_modified','2026-01-08T12:44:38'),(1504,235,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min.jpg'),(1505,235,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:721;s:6:\"height\";i:748;s:4:\"file\";s:45:\"2025/12/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:150123;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:45:\"Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-289x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:289;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:35393;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:45:\"Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10579;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(1506,236,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-1.jpg'),(1507,236,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:721;s:6:\"height\";i:748;s:4:\"file\";s:47:\"2025/12/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-1.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:150123;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:47:\"Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-1-289x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:289;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:35393;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:47:\"Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min-1-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10579;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(1508,235,'_xva_source_media_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min.jpg'),(1509,235,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Jakob Roepke'),(1510,233,'_thumbnail_id','235'),(1511,233,'portrait','235'),(1512,233,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(1513,236,'_xva_source_media_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Jakob-Roepke-Coll-Nr-922-2009-min.jpg'),(1514,233,'intro','Bio Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, [&hellip;]'),(1515,236,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Jakob Roepke'),(1516,233,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(1517,233,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25484\" class=\"elementor elementor-25484\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore</p><p>Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, installation and digital technology as means to re-examine historical documents and their influence, so inviting audiences to contemplate the contradictions of how we record and understand history.</p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2008 MA (Hons.) Visual Arts, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2004 BFA, National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: “Lost Pages From One Thousand and One Nights, Canvas Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2019: “Dust to Dust” at Kang Contemporary Gallery, Berlin, DE.<br />2018: “Pasts in Particles ” at Twelve Twelve Gallery, Den Haag, NL.<br />2018: “Holy Water” Open Studio 2018, at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2017: “Light on the Fringe of Time” Open Studio at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2015: “Enclosure/Erasure”, solo show at Koel Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2013 Art Basel Hong Kong, Hong Kong<br />2012 Lik Likoti, Canvas Gallery, Karachi<br />2011 The Memory is the Message, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Twelve Gates Art Gallery, Philadelphia<br />2010 Badshahnama, Solo show at Tmproject Gallery Geneva</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2019: “Neighbourhoods and Communities” Sommerfest, at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2019: “Engaging with Histories” at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2019: “Badshahnama” 2 Person Show at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE.<br />2019: “Mera Safar” Koel Galleery Karachi, PK.<br />2018: “within /without ” Asia House London.UK.<br />2018: “Seen Unseen” Kasteel Oud-Rekem, BE.<br />2018: “Revelation: Reclaiming South Asian Narratives” exhibition and seminar at Harvard university, South Asia Institute, Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA.<br />2018: “Changing Places” Phoenix, Leicester, UK.<br />2017: “The Materiality of the Invisible” at Marres, Centre for Contemporary Culture Maastricht, NL.<br />2017: “The Great Wall” Karachi Biennale, PK.<br />2017: “Changing Places” Hastings Museum &amp; Art Gallery, UK.<br />2017: “Taqseem” koel gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2016: “The Materiality of the Invisible #01” at Jan Van Eyck Academie, Maastricht, NL.<br />2016: “Hopes of Paradise ”, at Grosvenor gallery London. UK.<br />2016: “Vanishing Point” Artport, Tel Aviv, IL.<br />2016: “IFAA Contemporary Project Phase I” at Solutions! Musee de L’Art et de I’Espace, Paris, FR.<br />2015: “The Lay of the Land”, at Gallery Latitude 28, New Delhi IND.<br />2015: “Art15 London”, with Khaas Gallery, UK.<br />2014: “SINDH Reverberating sounds echo through the dessert” at Koel Gallery, Karachi, PK.<br />2014: “I.D” at the Islamabad Literature Festival 2014 by MyArtWorld gallery, Islamabad, PK.<br />2014: “Stet”, at LLF, Alhamra art Gallery, Lahore, PK.<br />2013 27th Annual Exhibition of Punjab Art Association, Alhamra Arts Council, Lahore<br />2013 Paper, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2012 Faculty Show at Zahoor-ul-Akhlaq Gallery, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2012 Soul Searchers, 3 person show at Rohtas Gallery, Islamabad<br />2012 Band Baaja Baraat, IVS Gallery, Karachi<br />2011 The Return, 2nd International Festival of Contemporary Art, Museum of Modern &amp; Contemporary Art (MOMA), Algiers<br />2011 After All (curated by Quddus Mirza), Royat Gallery, Lahore<br />2011 Common Threads: Contemporary Art from Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Iran and Pakistan, Xerxes Gallery with NMart gallery at the Bastakiya at the Heritage House Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Finalist Exhibition of the Sovereign Asian Art Prize, The Rotunda, Hong Kong<br />2010 Contemporary Shahnama, millennium painting Exhibition, The Prince’s Foundation Gallery, London<br />2010 The Sovereign Asian Art Prize finalist exhibition, ARTSPACE, Helutrans, Singapore<br />2010 Creating Common Wealth, curated by Ragini Gallery, New Delhi, India<br />2010 Fatah Je Asay Pasay, Green Cardamom at V.M Art Gallery, Karachi &amp; Sindh Museum, Hyderabad<br />2010 Structures Within An Intervention, The Guild Art Gallery, New York<br />2010 Making of The History, Two person show, Canvas Gallery, Karachi<br />2010 The Havelian Express, CAIS Gallery, Hong Kong<br />2009 Tradition &amp; Tension, Art Scene Gallery, Karachi<br />2009 Redo Pakistan, a traveling show, Karachi, Lahore, Pakistan, England, UK, Dhaka, Bangladesh<br />2009 Starring: The Artist, Indus Valley Gallery, Karachi<br />2008 Degree show, Zahoor-ul-Akhalq Gallery, National college of Arts, Lahore<br />2008 Young Artist Exhibition, Alhmara Art Council, Lahore<br />2007 Dropping Tears Together, anokha laadla collective performance, Alhamra Art Council, Lahore<br />2006 Places Real and Imagined, Alhamra Art Gallery, Lahore<br />2005 Voices, Pakistan Development Forum, Islamabad</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a695bbd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a695bbd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Teaching Experience				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d28e438 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d28e438\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: Guest Teacher at Kinnard College for Women, Lahore. PK.<br />2021: Guest Teacher at Institute of Art and Design, University of Sindh, Jamshoro, PK.<br />2017: Guest Teacher at HKU – Beeldende Kunst, Utrecht, NL.<br />2007-2016: Assistant Professor in Department of Fine Arts at National College of Arts, Lahore, PK.<br />2915-16: External examiner for final year at Kinnard College for Women in Lahore, PK.<br />2015: Guest Teacher at Institute of Art &amp; design, Jamshoro, Sindh, PK.<br />2015: External examiner for final year at Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh, PK.<br />2012 : Guest Teacher Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh PK<br />2009 Workshop at Centre of Excellence Art &amp; Design Jamshoro, Sindh<br />2007-present National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-73afb86 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"73afb86\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Articles & Reviews				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-cb53373 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"cb53373\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Quddus Mirza, “ Back to Baghdad” The News newspaper, Pakistan, 24th October, 2021.<br />Numair A. Abbasi, “ The memory of objects” Daily Dawn newpaper, Pakistan. 7th November, 2021.<br />Salman Peerzada, “Lost and Found” Daily Dawn newpaper, Pakistan, 19th October, 2021.<br />Zahid Chaudhary, Itinerant Photography: Medium and Translation in the work of Imran Channa. “Photography in India: From Archives to Contemporary Practice” Published by Bloomsbury, USA.<br />“Dust to Dust” http://www.fvu.co.uk/projects/dust-to-dust<br />Ella Bjurman, About the Issue, Sindh Guardian, https://issuu.com/sapac/docs/sindh_guardian_<br />Iftikhar Dadi, Spectral Memories, Tanqeed, Magazine of art and culture. http://www.tanqeed.org/2016/03/enclosure- erasure-imran-channa/<br />Zarmeene’ Shah, The Hidden Truth, Herald, May 2015, Pakistan.<br />Iftikhar Dadi, Spectral Memories, Enclosure/Erasure exhibition catalogue. Lahore<br />Quddus Mirza, The art of disappearance, Encoure, The News, April 5, 2015. Pakistan.<br />Rabeya Jalil, Reviews: Reworking Memories and Histories, ArtNow Pakistan.<br />Sadia Salim, A journey into abstraction, Daily Dawn, Sunday, April 5, 2015, Pakistan.<br />Interview: Re-aligning historical perspective: in conversation with Amra Ali. Dawn, August 11, 2013.<br />Alina Husain, “Art as communication” Herald, February 2013,Karachi.<br />M. Saeed Qureshi, Elucidating illusion. Daily Dawn, January 19 , 2013, Karachi.<br />Peerzada Salman, Lik Likoti opens at Canvas, 19 Dec , 2012, Daily Dawn, Karachi.<br />Shahim AKhtar, Imran Channa, Lik LIkoti” Pakistan art Review, Karachi.<br />“The Memory is the Message” Al Itihad, Saturday , 11th June, UAE.<br />Meilz Manfred ed, Painting The Persian Book of Kings Today. Cambridge: Talking Tree Books.<br />Ansari, Saira. Three Blind Mice, Papercuts Vol 7. online magazine.<br />Khan Naiza h. 2010. The Rising Tide, The Rising Tide New Directions in art from Pakistan 1990-2010:Karachi, Mohatta Palace Museum.<br />Nasar Hammad. 2010. Engaging Urban Realities Through A ‘Thinking’ Photography. TheRisingTide New Directions in art from Pakistan 1990- 2010:Karachi, Mohatta Palace Museum.<br />Imran Khan!.2010. Myth and reality. Pakistan’s rising tide. AlJazeera. 2010.<br />Asim Akhtar. PAUSE PLAY. Libas international Magazine, Volume 23 issue 22010. Lahore.<br />Quddus Mirza. His pupil’s voice, The News. Jul 2010<br />Nasar Hammad. Fatah jay Aassay Paassay. In the Milieu of fatah Halepoto, published by Green Cardamom, London.<br />Adamjee, Maheen Bashir. Messages for the Discerning, NEWSLINE, 31 May, 2010, Karachi.<br />Ahmad H, Ameer. Nostalgia, experimentalism and political games: ‘Making of History/Green Patrol’. Daily Times, April 15, 2010, Karachi.<br />Yee-Wan Koon, Blindness and Insight, MUSE , February, 2010, Hong Kong.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-552072e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"552072e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Awards, Residencies & Fellowships				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c6b5a50 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c6b5a50\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021-22: Artist in Residence at EYE Filmmuseum, Amsterdam, NL.<br />2019-2020: Artist Fellowship at Akademie Schloss Solitude, Stuttgart, DE.<br />2018: Artist Fellowship at Harvard University South Asia Institute, Massachusetts, Boston, USA.<br />2018-21: Recipient of “Werkbijdrage Bewezen Talent” by Mondriaan Fonds. Amsterdam, NL.<br />2013 Award of Excellence, AAP Lahore<br />2011 Gasworks International Residency Programme, London<br />2010 Finalist for the Sovereign Asian Art Prize 2010, Hong Kong<br />2004 Merit scholarship, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2003 Merit scholarship, National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1518,233,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1519,233,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1520,233,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1521,233,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1522,233,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1523,233,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1524,233,'origin','Bio Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, [&hellip;]'),(1525,233,'origin','Bio Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, [&hellip;]'),(1526,233,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1527,233,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1528,233,'artwork_gallery','a:19:{i:0;i:235;i:1;i:824;i:2;i:825;i:3;i:826;i:4;i:827;i:5;i:828;i:6;i:829;i:7;i:830;i:8;i:831;i:9;i:832;i:10;i:833;i:11;i:834;i:12;i:835;i:13;i:836;i:14;i:837;i:15;i:838;i:16;i:839;i:17;i:840;i:18;i:841;}'),(1529,233,'artwork_gallery','a:19:{i:0;i:235;i:1;i:824;i:2;i:825;i:3;i:826;i:4;i:827;i:5;i:828;i:6;i:829;i:7;i:830;i:8;i:831;i:9;i:832;i:10;i:833;i:11;i:834;i:12;i:835;i:13;i:836;i:14;i:837;i:15;i:838;i:16;i:839;i:17;i:840;i:18;i:841;}'),(1530,233,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1531,233,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1532,237,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/artist/imran-channa/'),(1533,237,'_xva_source_id','25467'),(1534,237,'_xva_source_content','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25467\" class=\"elementor elementor-25467\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1981 Pakistan, lives in Lahore</p><p>Imran Channa is a Pakistani visual artist. Channa’s primary interest is in historical documentation and how that documentation creates narratives, information and misinformation. He finds that historical narratives and the documents that create or support them are limited in scope and complexity. He uses drawing, moving image, installation and digital technology as means to re-examine historical documents and their influence, so inviting audiences to contemplate the contradictions of how we record and understand history.</p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2008 MA (Hons.) Visual Arts, National College of Arts, Lahore<br />2004 BFA, National College of Arts, Lahore</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2021: “Lost Pages From One Thousand and One Nights, Canvas Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2019: “Dust to Dust” at Kang Contemporary Gallery, Berlin, DE.<br />2018: “Pasts in Particles ” at Twelve Twelve Gallery, Den Haag, NL.<br />2018: “Holy Water” Open Studio 2018, at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2017: “Light on the Fringe of Time” Open Studio at Jan van Eyck Academie, Maastricht. NL.<br />2015: “Enclosure/Erasure”, solo show at Koel Gallery Karachi, PK.<br />2013 Art Basel Hong Kong, Hong Kong<br />2012 Lik Likoti, Canvas Gallery, Karachi<br />2011 The Memory is the Message, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Twelve Gates Art Gallery, Philadelphia<br />2010 Badshahnama, Solo show at Tmproject Gallery Geneva</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b49a62b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"b49a62b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Select Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-