entor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"d912eb9\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in Austin, Texas to German parents; moved to Munich, Germany, at 8 years of age. Lives in Bed-Stuy, Brooklyn. Halona makes objects. Her work has been included in group and solo shows in Europe, the U.A.E. and New York. Halona co-founded Full Tank, an all-female experimental band with all original songs; her current band is Fetzig, also a DIY band.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1990 – 1995 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Hochschule der Bildenden Kuenste Saar, Saarbruecken, Germany<br />1994 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Nova Scotia College of Art and Design, Halifax, Canada</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>021 Halona Hilbertz: Fledgling Beasts, Sala Projects, New York, NY<br />2021 Sommerausstellung, Museum St. Wendel, Sankt Wendel, Germany<br />2020 Uncertainty, Viridian Artists Gallery, New York, NY<br />2019 Empathetic Dream Construction: Braithwaite, Hilbertz &amp; Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2018 The Doll Show, Ceres Gallery, New York, NY<br />2018 Small Works, Trestle Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2017 Europe in China: Contemporary Sculpture Exhibition from Germany, Austria and Switzerland, Qingdao Sculpture Museum, Qingdao, China<br />2017 Collectivity: Objects and Associations in the U.A.E. Art World, Maraya Art Centre, Sharjah, United Arab Emirates<br />2017 Culture of One, sTudio 7 Gallery, Fort Tilden, NY<br />2015 Dog, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2014 Curiouser and Curiouser: Halona Hilbertz, Colleen Quigley &amp; Jakob Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2013 13th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2012 12th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2011 Rendezvous: Exposition Internationale d’Art Contemporain en Region du Val de Loire (Catalogue) Domaine Saint Hilaire, Roiffe, France<br />2010 Creative Couples, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2010 11th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2009 10th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2008 Katja Fratzscher &amp; Halona Hilbertz: Zeichnungen &amp; Objekte, 2-person show, curated by Anna Schädlich, Q-Club, Berlin, Germany<br />2008 9th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Play, Proteus Gowanus, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Wish You Were Here, A.I.R. Gallery, New York, NY<br />2007 20 Birds (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2006 Laundry-Women-Art, Bliss Street Studio Gallery, Queens, NY<br />2006 Halona Hilbertz: Wall Dolls. Donn Davis: Collage Paintings. (Two Person Show) XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2006 Terrible Toy Fair III CBGB Art Gallery, New York, NY<br />2006 Cyclical States of Boredom in the Face of World Domination Rachel Mason’s Studio, Brooklyn, NY<br />2005 Pfiennale Pfiff Restaurant, New York, NY<br />2005 8th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 Dollhouses in the Dollhaus Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 P.M.S./Women Painters, Musicians and Sculptors, Brooklyn College Art Gallery at the Brooklyn War Memorial, NY<br />2004 7th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 Dollops, Knit Objects &amp; Wall Dolls (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 WACO Show 49 Ann, New York, NY<br />2003 New Art Show Hines Studios, Charleston, SC<br />2003 Everything Must Go (27-Artist Show, Co-Curated with Donn Davis, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, New York<br />2003 6th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2002 5th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2001 Williamsburg Arts and Culture Festival, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, NY<br />2000 Elsewhere Festival, In conjunction with Bernadette Salvage Fine Art, Brooklyn, NY<br />1997 Künstler machen Schilder für Rottweil (Catalogue), Forum Kunst, Rottweil, Germany<br />1997 Artoll Labor<br />1997 Rheinische Landesklinik, Bedburg-Hau, Germany<br />1996 Und tschüss! (Solo), Galerie Gabriele Hühnergarth, Merzig, Germany<br />1996 Zuviele Männchen Künstlerhaus Am Acker, Berlin, Germany<br />1995 393 Jahre Fotografie -10 Künstler x ein Medium (Catalogue), Saarländisches Künstlerhaus, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1995 Bel Etage (Postcard Edition), Wilhelm-Heinrich-Strasse 20, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1994 Position 94, Volkshochschulzentrum, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1993 Die Wortansammlung (Two Person Show, with Christian H. Cordes), Galerie Gabriele Huehnergarth, Merzig, Germany<br />1993 Innenraum – Aussenraum, Galerie Im Zwinger, St. Wendel, Germany<br />1993 Wir sind gerne hier Rathaus, Altenkessel, Germany<br />1992 Neue Medien – Klasse! (Catalogue), Saarländisches Künstlerhaus, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1991 10 x 10 (Catalogue), Kunsthaus, Wiesbaden, Germany</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8f0593e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"8f0593e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Performances				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-889d3ef elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"889d3ef\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>1998 Pseudo Studio Walk (Internet live broadcast)<br />Pseudo Programs, New York / Selected and funded by Franklin Furnace, New York, NY<br />1998 B.D.-N.Y.-B.D.: Eine Flasche geht auf Reisen (in: Das Bad Dürkheim Projekt), (Catalogue),Winzergenossenschaft, Bad Dürkheim, Germany<br />1996 Schlagsahne in die Magengrube (Artist Book Edition) Stadtmuseum, Gross-Gerau, Germany / Funded by Iniative GG-1973<br />1996 Kohlenhydrate Kochen (with Christian H. Cordes) (in: Murmeln und böse Nachbarn), Hochschule für Künste, Bremen, Germany<br />1996 Die Monogamie (Theaterperformance. Written, directed. Costumes and stage set designed &amp; produced. Peformed, with Susanne Wilms and Thomas Machel.) Hochschule der Bildenden Künste Saar, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1994 Disarming Moments (in: Disarming Moments) Eyelevel Gallery, Halifax, Canada<br />1994 Breathing (in: Breathing, Installation by Kirsten Forkert) Starracles Gallery, Halifax, Canada<br />1994 Gegacker (with Christian H. Cordes) Khyber Cafe, Halifax, Canada<br />1994 Anti-Feminist (in: Performance Evening) Nova Scotia College of Art &amp; Design, Halifax, Canada<br />1993 Gespenst in Strapsen (in: Innenraum – Aussenraum) Galerie Im Zwinger, St. Wendel, Germany<br />1993 Eine Mütze voll Charme (with Christian H. Cordes) Kapelle Gutenbrunn, Homburg, Germany<br />1992 Zwischenprüfungs performance Hochschule der Bildenden Künste Saar, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1992 Eric Satie: Méduse (Stageset and Costumes for event, with Leslie Huppert) Weltkulturerbe Völklinger Hütte: Gasgebläsehalle, Völklingen, Germany<br />1992 Mondphasen (with Leslie Huppert and Susanne Wilms) Bürgerpark, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1992 Katzenfutter-Kindheit (in: Simultanperformance 1992) Hochschule der Bildenden Künste Saar, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1991 Sad (in: Simultanperformance 1991) Hochschule der Bildenden Künste Saar, Saarbrücken, Germany</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-46277da elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"46277da\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Awards and Grants				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-aa7dee0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"aa7dee0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1997 Franklin Furnace Goes Virtual, Performance Grant Recipient, Franklin Furnace, New York, NY<br />1996 Klohaeuschen (“Kunst am Bau”), Festo KG, Rohrbach, Germany<br />1993 Robert-Shuman-Kunstpreis, Finalist, Kulturaemter Saarbruecken and Trier, Germany; Metz, France; and Luxembourg<br />1991 Internationale Plakate Wettbewerb, Finalist, Hochschule der Bildenden Kuenste Saar / the City of Saarbruecken, Germany</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1628,249,'_xva_source_modified','2025-12-17T11:24:42'),(1629,251,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/HHZ-049-imageInsect-5-2018-Fabric-polymer-clay-laminated-butterfly-wings-glass-metal-acrylic-polyester-stuffing-36-x-13-x-15-cm.jpg'),(1630,251,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:667;s:6:\"height\";i:1000;s:4:\"file\";s:139:\"2025/12/HHZ-049-imageInsect-5-2018-Fabric-polymer-clay-laminated-butterfly-wings-glass-metal-acrylic-polyester-stuffing-36-x-13-x-15-cm.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:105903;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:139:\"HHZ-049-imageInsect-5-2018-Fabric-polymer-clay-laminated-butterfly-wings-glass-metal-acrylic-polyester-stuffing-36-x-13-x-15-cm-200x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:200;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:6551;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:139:\"HHZ-049-imageInsect-5-2018-Fabric-polymer-clay-laminated-butterfly-wings-glass-metal-acrylic-polyester-stuffing-36-x-13-x-15-cm-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:3236;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:3:\"3.5\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:19:\"Canon PowerShot G12\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:10:\"1544373869\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:6:\"12.074\";s:3:\"iso\";s:3:\"800\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:4:\"0.05\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}s:3:\"alt\";s:0:\"\";}}'),(1631,251,'_xva_source_media_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/HHZ-049-imageInsect-5-2018-Fabric-polymer-clay-laminated-butterfly-wings-glass-metal-acrylic-polyester-stuffing-36-x-13-x-15-cm.jpg'),(1632,251,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Halona Hilbertz'),(1633,249,'_thumbnail_id','252'),(1634,249,'portrait','252'),(1635,249,'_portrait','field_xva_artist_portrait'),(1636,249,'intro','Bio Born in Austin, Texas to German parents; moved to Munich, Germany, at 8 years of age. Lives in Bed-Stuy, Brooklyn. Halona makes objects. Her work has been included in group and solo shows in Europe, the U.A.E. and New York. Halona co-founded Full Tank, an all-female experimental band with all original songs; her current [&hellip;]'),(1637,249,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(1638,249,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25429\" class=\"elementor elementor-25429\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d912eb9 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"d912eb9\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in Austin, Texas to German parents; moved to Munich, Germany, at 8 years of age. Lives in Bed-Stuy, Brooklyn. Halona makes objects. Her work has been included in group and solo shows in Europe, the U.A.E. and New York. Halona co-founded Full Tank, an all-female experimental band with all original songs; her current band is Fetzig, also a DIY band.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1990 – 1995 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Hochschule der Bildenden Kuenste Saar, Saarbruecken, Germany<br />1994 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Nova Scotia College of Art and Design, Halifax, Canada</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>021 Halona Hilbertz: Fledgling Beasts, Sala Projects, New York, NY<br />2021 Sommerausstellung, Museum St. Wendel, Sankt Wendel, Germany<br />2020 Uncertainty, Viridian Artists Gallery, New York, NY<br />2019 Empathetic Dream Construction: Braithwaite, Hilbertz &amp; Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2018 The Doll Show, Ceres Gallery, New York, NY<br />2018 Small Works, Trestle Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2017 Europe in China: Contemporary Sculpture Exhibition from Germany, Austria and Switzerland, Qingdao Sculpture Museum, Qingdao, China<br />2017 Collectivity: Objects and Associations in the U.A.E. Art World, Maraya Art Centre, Sharjah, United Arab Emirates<br />2017 Culture of One, sTudio 7 Gallery, Fort Tilden, NY<br />2015 Dog, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2014 Curiouser and Curiouser: Halona Hilbertz, Colleen Quigley &amp; Jakob Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2013 13th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2012 12th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2011 Rendezvous: Exposition Internationale d’Art Contemporain en Region du Val de Loire (Catalogue) Domaine Saint Hilaire, Roiffe, France<br />2010 Creative Couples, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2010 11th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2009 10th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2008 Katja Fratzscher &amp; Halona Hilbertz: Zeichnungen &amp; Objekte, 2-person show, curated by Anna Schädlich, Q-Club, Berlin, Germany<br />2008 9th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Play, Proteus Gowanus, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Wish You Were Here, A.I.R. Gallery, New York, NY<br />2007 20 Birds (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2006 Laundry-Women-Art, Bliss Street Studio Gallery, Queens, NY<br />2006 Halona Hilbertz: Wall Dolls. Donn Davis: Collage Paintings. (Two Person Show) XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2006 Terrible Toy Fair III CBGB Art Gallery, New York, NY<br />2006 Cyclical States of Boredom in the Face of World Domination Rachel Mason’s Studio, Brooklyn, NY<br />2005 Pfiennale Pfiff Restaurant, New York, NY<br />2005 8th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 Dollhouses in the Dollhaus Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 P.M.S./Women Painters, Musicians and Sculptors, Brooklyn College Art Gallery at the Brooklyn War Memorial, NY<br />2004 7th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 Dollops, Knit Objects &amp; Wall Dolls (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 WACO Show 49 Ann, New York, NY<br />2003 New Art Show Hines Studios, Charleston, SC<br />2003 Everything Must Go (27-Artist Show, Co-Curated with Donn Davis, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, New York<br />2003 6th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2002 5th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2001 Williamsburg Arts and Culture Festival, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, NY<br />2000 Elsewhere Festival, In conjunction with Bernadette Salvage Fine Art, Brooklyn, NY<br />1997 Künstler machen Schilder für Rottweil (Catalogue), Forum Kunst, Rottweil, Germany<br />1997 Artoll Labor<br />1997 Rheinische Landesklinik, Bedburg-Hau, Germany<br />1996 Und tschüss! (Solo), Galerie Gabriele Hühnergarth, Merzig, Germany<br />1996 Zuviele Männchen Künstlerhaus Am Acker, Berlin, Germany<br />1995 393 Jahre Fotografie -10 Künstler x ein Medium (Catalogue), Saarländisches Künstlerhaus, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1995 Bel Etage (Postcard Edition), Wilhelm-Heinrich-Strasse 20, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1994 Position 94, Volkshochschulzentrum, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1993 Die Wortansammlung (Two Person Show, with Christian H. Cordes), Galerie Gabriele Huehnergarth, Merzig, Germany<br />1993 Innenraum – Aussenraum, Galerie Im Zwinger, St. Wendel, Germany<br />1993 Wir sind gerne hier Rathaus, Altenkessel, Germany<br />1992 Neue Medien – Klasse! (Catalogue), Saarländisches Künstlerhaus, Saarbrücken, Germany<br />1991 10 x 10 (Catalogue), Kunsthaus, Wiesbaden, Germany</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8f0593e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"8f0593e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.