lude postmodern strategies of making in relation to themes of materiality, perception, memory and place, and the transcultural flow of objects. Her work [&hellip;]'),(1714,261,'_intro','field_xva_exhibition_intro'),(1715,261,'biography','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25365\" class=\"elementor elementor-25365\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Colleen Quigley is a Japanese-American visual artist based in Tucson, Arizona. Her practice encompasses a broad range of media including sculpture, installation, painting, encaustic, and digital fabrication. Colleen Quigley’s research interests include postmodern strategies of making in relation to themes of materiality, perception, memory and place, and the transcultural flow of objects. Her work has been exhibited in Italy, Japan, Singapore, the United States,<br />and the U.A.E.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1999.2001 New York Academy of Art, New York, New York, USA<br />Graduate studies in Figurative Painting<br />1987.1989 Tokyo National University of Fine Arts and Music, Tokyo, Japan<br />Master of Fine Arts in Printmaking<br />Recipient of Rotary Yoneyama Memorial Foundation Scholarship<br />1986.1987 Kyoto Institute of Technology, Kyoto, Japan<br />Recipient of a Japanese Government Scholarship (Monbusho) to research traditional and contemporary Japanese woodblock techniques.<br />1979.1983 University of the Arts, Philadelphia, Pa., USA<br />Bachelor of Fine Arts in Sculpture</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5966237 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"5966237\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2023 Upcoming – Solo Exhibition Mesa Art Museum, SRP Gallery, Mesa, AZ, USA<br />2018  XVA, Solo Exhibition, The Remarkable Resilience of Symbols, Dubai, UAE<br />2015 XVA Gallery, Searching for Optical Wonder, Dubai, UAE<br />2007 MORE 2, Dubai, UAE<br />2006 MORE, Subjects, Dubai, UAE,<br />1995 CLAY GALLERY, Objects of Desire, Ginza, Tokyo, Japan<br />1992 BRENDA HALL GALLERY, East Meets West, San Francisco, Calif., USA<br />1991 GALLERY MIHARAYA, Ginza, Tokyo, Japan<br />1989 GALLERY ARIES, Ginza, Tokyo, Japan<br />1988 TAMURA GALLERY, Kanda, Tokyo, Japan<br />1987 GALLERY BENI, Kyoto, Japan</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2023 Summer Allegory, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2022 Yun Gee Park Gallery, Stage(s)(ing), (three person exhibition)Tucson, AZ, USA<br />2021 XVA Gallery, A Summer Solstice, Dubai, UAE<br />2021 FOUND:RE Contemporary Gallery, XSCAPE, Landscapes, Cityscapes, Mindscapes, Phoenix, AZ, USA<br />2020 Mesa Contemporary Art Center 41st Annual Contemporary Craft Exhibition, Mesa, AZ<br />2019 Tohono Chul Gallery, Dia de Los Muertos, Tucson, AZ, USA<br />2018  Al Fonoun Gallery, A Place to be, A Place to See, A Place to Spend the day, Abu Dhabi, UAE<br />2017  Bennetton Art Project, Imago Mundi, Salo, Italy<br />2016   Art Dubai and Al Serkal Avenue, RCA Secret, Dubai, UAE<br />2015 Tashkeel, Sustaining Identity, Nad Al Sheba, Dubai, UAE<br />2015 Sikka Art Fair Engaged Territories, Al Fahidi District, Dubai, UAE<br />2015 RCA Secret Dubai, Dubai Art Fair, Dubai, UAE<br />2014 Cuadro Gallery – Streaming Pool, International Symposium of Electronic Art (ISEA) Dubai, UAE<br />2014 ISEA 2014, Nomadic Doll Exhibition, Zayed University, Dubai, UAE<br />2014 ISEA 2014, Tables of Curiosities, Zayed University, Dubai, UAE<br />2014 XVA Gallery – Curiouser and Curiouser, Dubai, UAE<br />2013 Al Fonoun Gallery, Zayed University, Desert Pop, Abu Dhabi, UAE<br />2013 XVA Art Hotel, The Infusion of Impossible Things, Al Fahidi District, Dubai, UAE<br />2012 FN Gallery, Crossing the Emirates II, Dubai, UAE<br />2012 XVA, To the Moon, Sikka Art Fair, Dubai, UAE<br />2011 JAMJAR, Muqtanayati II– One Hundred Treasures, Dubai, UAE<br />2011 INDEX 2011, JAM JAR, Dubai, UAE<br />2011 TASHKEEL, Made in Tashkeel, Dubai, UAE<br />2011 ZAYED UNIVERSITY ATRIUM – Crossing the Emirates, Dubai, UAE<br />2011 TASHKEEL, As the Saying Goes, Dubai, UAE<br />2010 JAMJAR, Muqtanayati – One Hundred Treasures, Dubai, UAE<br />2010 XVA Summer Collection, Dubai, UAE<br />2010 TASHKEEL, Portrait of a Generation, Dubai, UAE<br />2010 BASTAKIYA ART FAIR, Nishan, Dubai, UAE<br />2010 BASTAKIYA ART FAIR, Plush Doll curatorial project, Dubai, UAE<br />2009 XVA Summer Show, Dubai, UAE<br />2009 Emerge – Ways of Worldmaking, San Servolo Palazzina 11, Isola di San Servolo, Venice, Italy<br />2009 BASTAKIYA ART FAIR, Dubai, UAE<br />2009 TASHKEEL, Silent Conversations, Dubai, UAE<br />2008 JAM JAR, In Situ, Dubai, UAE<br />2008 XVA Creek Art Fair, In the Mix, Dubai, UAE<br />2008 JAM JAR, Creek Art Fair, Constructing the Constructor, Dubai, UAE<br />2008 TASHKEEL, Vibrations Within, Dubai, UAE<br />2007 ART ATTACK, Minus-Reality, Dubai, UAE<br />2007 MEEM GALLERY, Rtoosh, Dubai, UAE<br />2003 THE COLLEGE OF WOOSTER ART MUSEUM, Ebert Art Center, Wooster, Ohio<br />2000 NATIONAL ARTS CLUB, New York Academy of Art Group Show, New York, USA<br />1995 LITHUANIA ARTISTS PALACE, Vilnius, Lithuania.<br />Women Step East to West – Traveling exhibition featuring women’s art in Japan, sponsored by the Japan Foundation in coordination with Gallery Lunami, Tokyo, Japan<br />1991 SAN FRANCISCO WOMEN’S ART GALLERY, San Francisco, Ca., USA<br />1989 TOKYO NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS &amp; MUSIC GALLERY, Foreign Artists Exhibition, Tokyo, Japan.<br />1988 MACHIDA MUSEUM, Student Printmaking Show, Tokyo, Japan.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8f0593e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"8f0593e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Public Collections				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-889d3ef elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"889d3ef\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>LA SERRE BISTRO, VIDA HOTEL, Downtown Dubai, UAE<br />XVA Gallery, Dubai, UAE<br />TASHKEEL, Dubai, UAE<br />MORE CAFÉ, Dubai, UAE<br />MONSANTO CORPORATION, Tokyo, Japan<br />AOYAMA COSMOS CORPORATION, Tokyo, Japan<br />I.M.I. CORPORATION, Tokyo, Japan<br />TOWN JUKU, INC., Tokyo, Japan<br />URAWA BUDDHIST TEMPLE, Urawa, Tokyo, Japan<br />WOZEN RESTAURANT, Tokyo, Japan<br />SAINOHIRA SENBEI, INC., Tokyo, Japan<br />BRENDA HALL GALLERY, San Francisco, Calif., USA</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1716,261,'_biography','field_xva_artist_biography'),(1717,261,'artist_statement','<p></p>'),(1718,261,'_artist_statement','field_xva_artist_statement'),(1719,261,'origin','bio Colleen Quigley is a Japanese-American visual artist based in Tucson, Arizona. Her practice encompasses a broad range of media including sculpture, installation, painting, encaustic, and digital fabrication. Colleen Quigley’s research interests include postmodern strategies of making in relation to themes of materiality, perception, memory and place, and the transcultural flow of objects. Her work [&hellip;]'),(1720,261,'_origin','field_xva_artist_origin'),(1721,261,'artwork_gallery','a:9:{i:0;i:263;i:1;i:490;i:2;i:898;i:3;i:899;i:4;i:900;i:5;i:901;i:6;i:902;i:7;i:903;i:8;i:904;}'),(1722,261,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(1723,264,'_xva_source_media_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CQ-120-imageSpring-2024-Heat-formed-laser-cut-cast-acrylic-99-x-89-x-28cm-scaled.png'),(1724,264,'_wp_attachment_image_alt','Colleen Quigley'),(1725,63,'_wp_old_date','2026-08-20'),(1726,265,'_thumbnail_id','124'),(1727,265,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1728,265,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"xva-mockup-single-artist\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"shortcode\",\"settings\":{\"shortcode\":\"[xva_mockup_single type=\\\"artist\\\"]\"},\"elements\":[]}]'),(1729,265,'_elementor_page_assets','a:1:{s:7:\"scripts\";a:1:{i:0;s:18:\"elementor-frontend\";}}'),(1730,265,'_elementor_css','a:7:{s:4:\"time\";i:1787257961;s:5:\"fonts\";a:0:{}s:5:\"icons\";a:0:{}s:20:\"dynamic_elements_ids\";a:0:{}s:6:\"status\";s:5:\"empty\";i:0;s:0:\"\";s:3:\"css\";s:0:\"\";}'),(1731,265,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.2.3:4.2.1:7648e729aae38c0825752571ace57347'),(1732,265,'_elementor_element_cache','{\"timeout\":1787344362,\"value\":{\"content\":\"[elementor-element k=\"f85d86bc5c2d4d02849e43047cec400b\" data=\"eyJpZCI6Inh2YS1tb2NrdXAtc2luZ2xlLWFydGlzdCIsImVsVHlwZSI6IndpZGdldCIsInNldHRpbmdzIjp7InNob3J0Y29kZSI6Ilt4dmFfbW9ja3VwX3NpbmdsZSB0eXBlPVwiYXJ0aXN0XCJdIn0sImVsZW1lbnRzIjpbXSwid2lkZ2V0VHlwZSI6InNob3J0Y29kZSJ9\"]\",\"scripts\":[],\"styles\":[]}}'),(1733,63,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/artist/charlie-koolhaas/'),(1734,63,'_xva_source_id','25350'),(1735,63,'_xva_source_content','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25350\" class=\"elementor elementor-25350\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				about the artist				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>For over twenty years, Charlie Koolhaas’ exhibitions have been immersive landscapes you can enter and explore – places where flat images are folded into three-dimensional structures offering infinite perspectives. Charlie has authored various books that tell sociological stories by merging her images and writing into unified narratives. In 2020 she released her book City Lust, which combines writing and photography to take the viewer on a journey through the global economy. Her recently launched Foto-Couture, which makes her prints wearable, further frees her photographs from the boundaries of art institutions allowing them to enter the world where their meaning continues to evolve. Charlie has taught media theory and photography in various academic institutions such as Eindhoven School of design, TUDelft and the Sandberg Academy, and she has been a visiting lecturer at Harvard Graduate School of Design, ETH Zurich and The Architectural Association London.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		'),(1736,63,'_xva_source_modified','2025-12-17T10:54:56'),(1737,266,'_wp_attached_file','2025/12/CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1.jpg'),(1738,266,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1675;s:6:\"height\";i:2560;s:4:\"file\";s:86:\"2025/12/CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:530494;s:5:\"sizes\";a:10:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:86:\"CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1-196x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:196;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:10863;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:87:\"CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1-670x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:670;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:105281;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:86:\"CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5445;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:87:\"CK05-imageUntitled-City-Lust-Series-UV-print-on-dibond-28-x-40-cm-scaled-1-768x1174.jpg\";s:5:\"widt