trong></p>\n<p>[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]</p>\n<div>“It is a truism to observe that a cascade of big issues now dominates our lives. Social media, TV, radio and print scream dystopian stories at us 24/7. We are suffering far less than in the past from war, disease or famine but we are always in crisis and in a constant state of anxiety. Crowds hold up placards somewhere every day as civil protest remains a vital democratic tool for people to have their say.<span class=\"gmail-Apple-converted-space\"> </span></div>\n<div></div>\n<div> These artworks reflect the zeitgeist of an era.”<span class=\"gmail-Apple-converted-space\"> </span>&#8211; Mukesh Shah</div>\n<div></div>\n<div> The artist’s solo show at XVA Gallery is titled<span class=\"gmail-Apple-converted-space\"> </span>C?N U FEEL IT<span class=\"gmail-Apple-converted-space\"> </span>after his first monograph published by Akkadia Press this year. It showcases Shah&#8217;s insightful work, where he paints a thousand pictures with his created slogans, proving the extent to which words are capable of conveying the dystopian reality of this age.</div>\n<p>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][dfd_simple_image_gallery dfd_layer_image=&#8221;22533,22532,22531,22530,22529,22528,22527,22526,22525,22524,22523,22522,22521,22520,22519,22518,22517,22516,22515,22514,22513,22512,22511,22510,22509,22508&#8243; items_offset=&#8221;0&#8243; image_width=&#8221;900&#8243; image_height=&#8221;600&#8243; slides_to_show=&#8221;3&#8243; slides_to_scroll=&#8221;1&#8243; carousel_slideshow_speed=&#8221;3000&#8243; images_style=&#8221;carousel&#8221;][/vc_column][/vc_row]</p>\n'),(2953,376,'_curatorial_text','field_xva_exhibition_curatorial_text'),(2954,376,'artwork_gallery','a:1:{i:0;i:377;}'),(2955,376,'_artwork_gallery','field_xva_exhibition_artwork_gallery'),(2956,376,'venue','XVA Gallery'),(2957,376,'_venue','field_xva_exhibition_venue'),(2958,378,'_xva_source_url','https://www.xvagallery.com/exhibitions/tempo/'),(2959,378,'_xva_source_id','21783'),(2960,378,'_xva_source_content','<p>Oussama Garti&#8217;s monochromatic works capture moments and emotions he deems are crucial to ‘trap’ in his sculpted drapes using fabric, needles, and many layers of liquified plaster that he then carefully sands.</p>\n<p><strong>Oussama Garti, September 23rd &#8211; November 4th 2021</strong></p>\n'),(2961,378,'_xva_source_modified','2021-09-28T10:21:08'),(2962,379,'_wp_attached_file','2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM.jpg'),(2963,379,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1184;s:6:\"height\";i:788;s:4:\"file\";s:48:\"2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:538135;s:5:\"sizes\";a:6:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:48:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:13544;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:49:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-1024x682.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:682;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:73580;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:48:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:6974;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:48:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-768x511.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:511;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:49522;}s:12:\"xva-portrait\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:49:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-1000x788.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1000;s:6:\"height\";i:788;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:84562;}s:8:\"xva-card\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:48:\"Screen-Shot-2021-09-28-at-2.00.59-PM-900x788.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:900;s:6:\"height\";i:788;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:80214;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:13:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s