A Gallery, Al Fahidi\"\n					aria-label=\"XVA Gallery, Al Fahidi\"\n			></iframe>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c2d65db e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"c2d65db\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-82466e3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"82466e3\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n					<h1 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">XVA Gallery</h1>				</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-017005b elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"017005b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n					<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Al Fahidi Neighborhood, Bur Dubai<br>\nP.O. Box 37304<br>\nDubai, UAE</h2>				</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6d6a1c0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"6d6a1c0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n					<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Email: <a href=\"mailto:xva@xvagallery.com\">xva@xvagallery.com</a><br>\nPhone: +9714 3535383<br>\nFax: +9714 3535988</h2>				</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ad931dc elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"ad931dc\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n					<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\"><b>OPENING HOURS:</b><br>\n7 days a week: 10am – 6pm<br>\nAnd by appointment outside of working hours.</h2>				</div>\n				</div>\n					</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Contact','<p>XVA Gallery Al Fahidi Neighborhood, Bur Dubai P.O. Box 37304 Dubai, UAE Email: xva@xvagallery.com Phone: +9714 3535383 Fax: +9714 3535988 OPENING HOURS: 7 days a</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','contact','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?page_id=10',0,'page','',0),(11,0,'2020-08-21 15:39:33','2026-08-20 18:37:56','<p>[vc_row css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598024447985{padding-top: 5% !important;}&#8221;][vc_column width=&#8221;2/3&#8243;][dfd_single_image image=&#8221;22553&#8243;][/vc_column][vc_column width=&#8221;1/3&#8243; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1651832931976{padding-right: 30px !important;padding-left: 30px !important;}&#8221; col_shadow=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C0.35)&#8221; col_shadow_hover=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C0.35)&#8221;][dfd_heading style=&#8221;style_02&#8243; subtitle=&#8221;&#8221; content_alignment=&#8221;text-left&#8221; enable_delimiter=&#8221;&#8221; undefined=&#8221;&#8221; title_font_options=&#8221;tag:h5&#8243; subtitle_font_options=&#8221;tag:div&#8221; title_google_fonts=&#8221;yes&#8221; title_custom_fonts=&#8221;font_family:Prata%3Aregular|font_style:400%20regular%3A400%3Anormal&#8221;]XVA Hotel[/dfd_heading][vc_separator color=&#8221;black&#8221; align=&#8221;align_left&#8221; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598021087516{padding-top: 10px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;}&#8221;][vc_column_text]The Al Fahidi Neighborhood, formerly known as Al Bastakiya, is Dubai’s oldest area and a former prominent trader’s settlement, near the Dubai Fort. Hidden in the heart of the historical Al Fahidi, in the maze-like sikkas or alleyways, on the colorful and soulful Dubai Creek, XVA Art Hotel is the former home of the Seddiqi family (Dubai’s Rolex dealers) &#8211; turned-boutique-hotel in the early 2000s by founder, Mona Hauser. XVA has created a niche and continues to facilitate conversations on art, culture, heritage and creativity for Dubai.</p>\n<p>Offering 15 individually designed suites and rooms, an award-winning restaurant, wind towers and three courtyards, this centrally located hotspot is the city’s unique retreat and best kept secret.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598024417327{padding-top: 50px !important;padding-bottom: 5% !important;}&#8221;][vc_column width=&#8221;2/3&#8243;][dfd_single_image image=&#8221;20903&#8243;][/vc_column][vc_column width=&#8221;1/3&#8243; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598024430106{padding-top: 5% !important;padding-right: 30px !important;padding-left: 30px !important;}&#8221; col_shadow=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C.35)&#8221; col_shadow_hover=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C.35)&#8221;][dfd_heading style=&#8221;style_02&#8243; subtitle=&#8221;&#8221; content_alignment=&#8221;text-left&#8221; enable_delimiter=&#8221;&#8221; undefined=&#8221;&#8221; title_font_options=&#8221;tag:h5&#8243; subtitle_font_options=&#8221;tag:div&#8221; title_google_fonts=&#8221;yes&#8221; title_custom_fonts=&#8221;font_family:Prata%3Aregular|font_style:400%20regular%3A400%3Anormal&#8221;]Café[/dfd_heading][vc_separator color=&#8221;black&#8221; align=&#8221;align_left&#8221; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598021095825{padding-top: 10px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;}&#8221;][vc_column_text]In the time since XVA Cafe has been open it has been hailed as ‘Dubai’s best kept secret’. The café serves freshly-prepared vegetarian and vegan food including a variety of main courses accompanied by salads, soups and desserts. Our chefs strive to constantly innovate their culinary vision through different cultures appealing to all pallets.<br />\nWe welcome you to enjoy a refreshing mint lemonade in our green and cozy courtyard, away from the hustle and bustle of the city.<br />\nXVA cafe is open daily from 7 am to 10 pm.[/vc_column_text][vc_empty_space height=&#8221;35px&#8221;][vc_btn title=&#8221;Visit XVA Hotel &amp; Café website&#8221; style=&#8221;outline-custom&#8221; outline_custom_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; outline_custom_hover_background=&#8221;#184255&#8243; outline_custom_hover_text=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; shape=&#8221;square&#8221; align=&#8221;left&#8221; link=&#8221;url:https%3A%2F%2Fwww.xvahotel.com%2F|target:_blank&#8221;][/vc_column][/vc_row]</p>\n','Hotel & Café','<p>[vc_row css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1598024447985{padding-top: 5% !important;}&#8221;][vc_column width=&#8221;2/3&#8243;][dfd_single_image image=&#8221;22553&#8243;][/vc_column][vc_column width=&#8221;1/3&#8243; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1651832931976{padding-right: 30px !important;padding-left: 30px !important;}&#8221; col_shadow=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C0.35)&#8221; col_shadow_hover=&#8221;box_shadow_enable:disable|shadow_horizontal:0|shadow_vertical:15|shadow_blur:50|shadow_spread:0|box_shadow_color:rgba(0%2C0%2C0%2C0.35)&#8221;][dfd_heading style=&#8221;style_02&#8243; subtitle=&#8221;&#8221; content_alignment=&#8221;text-left&#8221; enable_delimiter=&#8221;&#8221; undefined=&#8221;&#8221; title_font_options=&#8221;tag:h5&#8243; subtitle_font_options=&#8221;tag:div&#8221; title_google_fonts=&#8221;yes&#8221; title_custom_fonts=&#8221;font_family:Prata%3Aregular|font_style:400%20regular%3A400%3Anormal&#8221;]XVA Hotel[/dfd_heading][vc_separator color=&#8221;black&#8221;</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','hotel-cafe','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?page_id=11',0,'page','',0),(14,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:56','2026-08-20 18:37:56','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we are</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Our website address is: http://localhost:8090.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Comments</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>When visitors leave comments on the site we collect the data shown in the comments form, and also the visitor&#8217;s IP address and browser user agent string to help spam detection.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An anonymized string created from your email address (also called a hash) may be provided to the Gravatar service to see if you are using it. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/. After approval of your comment, your profile picture is visible to the public in the context of your comment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you upload images to the website, you should avoid uploading images with embedded location data (EXIF GPS) included. Visitors to the website can download and extract any location data from images on the website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cookies</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment on our site you may opt-in to saving your name, email address and website in cookies. These are for your convenience so that you do not have to fill in your details again when you leave another comment. These cookies will last for one year.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you visit our login page, we will set a temporary cookie to determine if your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your browser.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you log in, we will also set up several cookies to save your login information and your screen display choices. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for a year. If you select &quot;Remember Me&quot;, your login will persist for two weeks. If you log out of your account, the login cookies will be removed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you edit or publish an article, an additional cookie will be saved in your browser. This cookie includes no personal data and simply indicates the post ID of the article you just edited. It expires after 1 day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Embedded content from other websites</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Articles on this site may include embedded content (e.g. videos, images, articles, etc.). Embedded content from other websites behaves in the exact same way as if the visitor has visited the other website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These websites may collect data about you, use cookies, embed additional third-party tracking, and monitor your interaction with that embedded content, including tracking your interaction with the embedded content if you have an account and are logged in to that website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we share your data with</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you request a password reset, your IP address will be included in the reset email.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How long we retain your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained indefinitely. This is so we can recognize and approve any follow-up comments automatically instead of holding them in a moderation queue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For users that register on our website (if any), we also store the personal information they provide in their user profile. All users can see, edit, or delete their personal information at any time (except they cannot change their username). Website administrators can also see and edit that information.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What rights you have over your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you have an account on this site, or have left comments, you can request to receive an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, including any data you have provided to us. You can also request that we erase any personal data we hold about you. This does not include any data we are obliged to keep for administrative, legal, or security purposes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where your data is sent</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Visitor comments may be checked through an automated spam detection service.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n','Privacy Policy','','inherit','closed','closed','','3-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:37:56','2026-08-20 18:37:56','',3,'http://localhost:8090/?p=14',0,'revision','',0),(15,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:56','2026-08-20 18:37:56','','XVA Global Header','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-global-header','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-global-header',0,'elementor_library','',0),(16,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Global Footer','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-global-footer','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-global-footer',0,'elementor_library','',0),(17,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Fullscreen Menu','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-fullscreen-menu','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-fullscreen-menu',0,'elementor_library','',0),(18,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Artist Page Template','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-artist-page-template','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-artist-page-template',0,'elementor_library','',0),(19,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Exhibition Page Template','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-exhibition-page-template','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-exhibition-page-template',0,'elementor_library','',0),(20,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Artists Archive','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-artists-archive','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-artists-archive',0,'elementor_library','',0),(21,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Exhibitions Archive','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-exhibitions-archive','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-exhibitions-archive',0,'elementor_library','',0),(22,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA 404','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-404','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-404',0,'elementor_library','',0),(23,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Artist Loop Card','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-artist-loop-card','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-artist-loop-card',0,'elementor_library','',0),(24,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Exhibition Loop Card','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-exhibition-loop-card','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-exhibition-loop-card',0,'elementor_library','',0),(25,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','XVA Press Loop Card','','publish','closed','closed','','xva-press-loop-card','','','2026-08-20 19:21:41','2026-08-20 19:21:41','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?elementor_library=xva-press-loop-card',0,'elementor_library','',0),(26,0,'2025-12-17 11:27:05','2026-08-20 18:37:57','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25437\" class=\"elementor elementor-25437\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them. Interchangeably, sufi teachings are generally identified as highly individualistic and harmonious practices while being on the contrary- Observing the sporadic existence of dervish from the rise of sufism centuries ago,having being taken a vow of selfless love and distancing from the norms of society, they were and until now are deemed as controversial figures. Their presence brings uneasiness in social settings and questions the elaborate ways of the tediously complicated belief system. Similar to the silent uneasiness I try to achieve through my practice. </p><p>Manifesting creatures like bees, birds and fish as symbols for their inter-religious references, geo-location and life cycle. Ornate and complex geometric drawings hailing from centuries of tradition of being adorned with natural pigments and organic materials, whilst I choose to treat them with fluorescent colors that are industrially made and artificial in nature implying towards the need of beliefs becoming more synthetic and fabricated rather than being the innate desire to be spiritual and organic. Consistently moving between these ideas the imagery stands as a metaphor and holds a multitude of meaning. Actions like shredding and restructuring pages from history books, reducing words from letters to dots (nuqta). Coming forth as a process of unlearning a plethora of information being fed over a period of time. In totality my practice melts down to a consistent effort in breaking down or simplifying the complexity of fabricated information into the importance of one single entity. One minimal existence that contains all.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>BFA National College of Arts Lahore Pakistan</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2024- Art as process at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2024- Fronde Sance at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2023- What the land knows the hearts remember, four person at ArtSoch Gallery, Lahore, Pakistan<br />2023- Neon Equilibrium Virtual NFTs Morrow Collective 2022- Made in Tashkeel 22, Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Into the revolution, at Foundry downtown<br />Dubai. curated by Morrow collective<br />2021- Solstice at XVA gallery, Dubai UAE<br />2021- Made in Tashkeel 2021, at Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Genesis online NFT show curated by Morrow collective UAE<br />2021- Silent Confabulations, solo show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is at Alliance Francaise Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is part1 at Beit funn Dubai sustainable city, Dubai UAE<br />2020- Wolf tone at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2019- Made in Tashkeel 2019 at Tashkeel Dubai,UAE<br />2018- Made-in Tashkeel 2018 At Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2013- The Bear Show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Huma Shoaib','<p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them.</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','huma-shoaib','','','2026-08-21 05:49:21','2026-08-21 05:49:21','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?xva_artist=huma-shoaib',0,'xva_artist','',0),(27,0,'2026-08-06 11:10:04','2026-08-20 18:37:57','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"26524\" class=\"elementor elementor-26524\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9c0535e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9c0535e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2bc27a2 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2bc27a2\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>To forget is not only to lose. Oblivion is also where the mind makes room; clearing space for what matters now, letting go of what no longer serves. The works gathered here treat forgetting as a generative act: a hairbrush, an armchair, each object caught mid-transformation, shedding one meaning to make way for another.</p><p>Working across metal, textile, found and fabricated materials, the artists in this exhibition ask what becomes possible once memory stops holding on so tightly. Domestic and bodily objects are freed from their original function, made strange, playful, ornamental, evidence not of loss but of renewal, of a self continually remaking itself. Nothing here mourns the past. It repurposes it.</p><p>Forgetting, in this light, is less erasure than editing: a structural condition of how identity stays alive, how history keeps moving, how images and objects find new use once their first purpose has passed. What remains in these works is not absence but possibility: gesture freed from context, object freed from owner, form open to whatever meaning arrives next.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-83ab635 elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\" data-id=\"83ab635\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"button.default\">\n										<a class=\"elementor-button elementor-button-link elementor-size-sm\" href=\"#\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n						<span class=\"elementor-button-content-wrapper\">\n									<span class=\"elementor-button-text\">View Press Release</span>\n					</span>\n					</a>\n								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-863a80f elementor-hidden-desktop elementor-hidden-tablet elementor-hidden-mobile_extra elementor-hidden-mobile elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"863a80f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Bio</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-eda4a53 elementor-widget__width-inherit elementor-hidden-desktop elementor-hidden-tablet elementor-hidden-mobile_extra elementor-hidden-mobile elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"eda4a53\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in Edinburgh in 1976 and raised in Hong Kong, Jane Bailey Beveridge is a visual artist and dedicated art educator based in Dubai. She studied Graphic Design and Fine Art at the University of Brighton, graduating in 1998. In 2002, she joined the Art Department at Dubai College, where she has served as Head of Art since 2007.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Oblivion','<p>Join us for Oblivion, our summer exhibition, running from 28 July to 15 August 2026.</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','oblivion','','','2026-08-21 05:47:40','2026-08-21 05:47:40','',0,'http://localhost:8090/?xva_exhibition=oblivion',0,'xva_exhibition','',0),(28,0,'2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','','Default Kit','','inherit','closed','closed','','4-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:37:57','2026-08-20 18:37:57','',4,'http://localhost:8090/?p=28',0,'revision','',0),(29,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','5-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',5,'http://localhost:8090/?p=29',0,'revision','',0),(30,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Artists','','inherit','closed','closed','','6-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',6,'http://localhost:8090/?p=30',0,'revision','',0),(31,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Exhibitions','','inherit','closed','closed','','7-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',7,'http://localhost:8090/?p=31',0,'revision','',0),(32,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Art Consultancy','','inherit','closed','closed','','8-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',8,'http://localhost:8090/?p=32',0,'revision','',0),(33,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Press','','inherit','closed','closed','','9-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',9,'http://localhost:8090/?p=33',0,'revision','',0),(34,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Contact','','inherit','closed','closed','','10-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',10,'http://localhost:8090/?p=34',0,'revision','',0),(35,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','','Hotel & Café','','inherit','closed','closed','','11-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:39:50','2026-08-20 18:39:50','',11,'http://localhost:8090/?p=35',0,'revision','',0),(38,0,'2026-08-20 18:39:51','2026-08-20 18:39:51','','XVA Global Header','','inherit','closed','closed','','15-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 18:3