er\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>2022 59th La Biennale di Venezia<br />Personal Structures<br />2022 Palazzo Mora, Venice</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-fa4ba4b elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"fa4ba4b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				PUBLICATIONS				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-331ac09 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"331ac09\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>C?N U FEEL IT, Published by Akkadia Press, Edinburgh</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Mukesh Shah','<p>Mukesh Shah is a multi-disciplinary visual artist whose practice is a dialogue between contemplative abstraction focused on materiality and language-based works that explore contemporary issues.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','199-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:10','2026-08-20 21:01:10','',199,'http://localhost:8090/?p=210',0,'revision','',0),(211,0,'2025-12-17 12:42:28','2025-12-17 12:42:28','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25581\" class=\"elementor elementor-25581\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Mohammad Ali Talpur was born in 1976 in Tando Jam, Sindh.</p><p>He spent his childhood in his home town Tando Jam then he moved to Lahore. He got his BFA degree in 1998 from the National College of Arts, Lahore. He is teaching at National College of Arts and works at his studio in Lahore.</p><p>His work passed through various phases to get its unique identity. He is known for his linear drawings, and these drawings reflect the magical quality that a viewer can not resist to pass through the inner essence of visual pleasure. He creates drawings like poetry by arranging the cluster of lines on paper and deliberately states “art without content” which interpret the existence of life.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Mohammad Ali Talpur','<p>He got his BFA degree in 1998 from the National College of Arts, Lahore. He is teaching at National College of Arts and works at his studio in Lahore.</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','mohammad-ali-talpur','','','2026-08-21 05:48:48','2026-08-21 05:48:48','',0,'http://localhost:8090/artist/mohammad-ali-talpur/',0,'xva_artist','',0),(212,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:12','2026-08-20 21:01:12','','Mohammad Ali Talpur','','inherit','open','closed','','mohammad-ali-talpur-2','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MAT-7-imageLeeka-2014-Signed-dated-Ink-on-paper-32-x-24-cm-scaled-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(213,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:13','2026-08-20 21:01:13','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25595\" class=\"elementor elementor-25595\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				About the Artist				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Morvarid Mohammad is a sixteen-year-old Afghan-Iranian visual artist, illustrator, writer, and translator based in the UAE. Recognized as a versatile talent in contemporary art, she works with oil, watercolor, house paint, digital art, and graffiti. Her innovative use of house paint and loose digital illustrations convey a childlike yet complex perspective on cultural identity and nature.</p></div><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-70e7c24 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"70e7c24\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>As an emerging artist, Morvarid experiments with new mediums while evolving her unique style. She’s also an accomplished writer, exploring diverse topics in her articles and learning French to deepen her cultural repertoire. Engaged in her community, Morvarid participates in exhibitions, where her emotive work continues to inspire audiences.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ab552d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6ab552d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a342d24 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"a342d24\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f2779ab e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"f2779ab\" data-element_type=\"container\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ccba92a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ccba92a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>TCCF Solo Exhibition | June 9th 2021 – June 12th 2021<br />RAK Fine Arts Festival 2022 | February 4th – May 31st 2022<br />Tashkeel ‘Made in Tashkeel’ 2022 | June 28th – August 31st 2022<br />Moon Art Fair Hamburg 2022 | October 28th – 30th 2022 THIRST For Humanity 2022 | July 2nd – July 31st 2022<br />Art Juxtapose 2022 | June 30th – December 31st 2022 RAK Fine Arts Festival 2022 | February 4th – May 31st 2022 Artezaar | August 7th 2022<br />Artoze Global 2022 | August 20th 2022<br />Folx Gallery | August 29th 2022<br />The Ren House | September 29th 2022<br />Shop53 | October 22nd 2022<br />Sharjah Art Foundation | 25th – 27th November 2022<br />The Myriad | 25th November 2022<br />RAK Fine Arts Festival 2023 | 2nd February – 31st March 2023 Art Connects Women | 8th – 11th March 2023</p></div></div><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8dc1ec0 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"8dc1ec0\" data-element_type=\"container\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b4e0558 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"b4e0558\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>RAK Fine Arts Festival NFT Exhibition | 22nd March 2023<br />Tashkeel ‘Made in Tashkeel’ 2023 | 21st June – 5th September 2023<br />Sharjah Art Foundation Focal Point 2023 | 24th – 26th November 2023<br />Tashkeel ‘Made in Tashkeel’ 2024 | 11th June – 27th August 2024<br />Al Marsam Arts | 4th June – 4th July 2024<br />ICD Brookfield Place Souq Tasmeem Makers | 27th – 29th June 2024<br />RAK Art x Hilton Garden Inn Pop Up Exhibition | 25th July 2024<br />SheSays American University Dubai | 19th Octorber 2024<br />Fujairah Artist’s Street | 15th January 2024<br />RAK Art 2025 | 31ST January – 28TH February 2025<br />Sikka 2025 | 31st January – 9th February 2025<br />421 Abu Dhabi Workshop Instructor | 2nd February 2025 Art Dubai | 18th – 20th April 2025</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-42ffd8a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"42ffd8a\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-856da1e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"856da1e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-522b394 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"522b394\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Publications				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-205a35e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"205a35e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>The Nuances of New-Age Feminism 2022<br />Healthline Zine Issue 1 2022<br />Lines of Flight Issue 2 2022<br />Creative Guts Zine Issue 2022 Mulberry Literary Issue 2024</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c96ec15 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"c96ec15\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f71e16 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6f71e16\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Awards				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5995cff elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5995cff\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>SAE Institute University College | 3rd Prize Winner 2024 Little Strokes Academy | 3rd Prize Winner 2024 Regent Middle East | 1st Prize Winner 2024</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-af91e9c e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"af91e9c\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b4f959 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"9b4f959\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Grants & Memberships				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b013e30 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"b013e30\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8c3baf8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8c3baf8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\"><p>Art Jameel Research and Practice Platform | 9th September 2024<br />Fujairah Fine Arts Academy | 11TH February 2025</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Morvarid Mohammed','<p>As an emerging artist, Morvarid experiments with new mediums while evolving her unique style. She&#8217;s also an accomplished writer, exploring diverse topics in her articles and learning French to deepen her cultural repertoire. Engaged in her community, Morvarid participates in exhibitions, where her emotive work continues to inspire audiences.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','208-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:13','2026-08-20 21:01:13','',208,'http://localhost:8090/?p=213',0,'revision','',0),(214,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:15','2026-08-20 21:01:15','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25581\" class=\"elementor elementor-25581\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Mohammad Ali Talpur was born in 1976 in Tando Jam, Sindh.</p><p>He spent his childhood in his home town Tando Jam then he moved to Lahore. He got his BFA degree in 1998 from the National College of Arts, Lahore. He is teaching at National College of Arts and works at his studio in Lahore.</p><p>His work passed through various phases to get its unique identity. He is known for his linear drawings, and these drawings reflect the magical quality that a viewer can not resist to pass through the inner essence of visual pleasure. He creates drawings like poetry by arranging the cluster of lines on paper and deliberately states “art without content” which interpret the existence of life.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Mohammad Ali Talpur','<p>He got his BFA degree in 1998 from the National College of Arts, Lahore. He is teaching at National College of Arts and works at his studio in Lahore.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','211-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:15','2026-08-20 21:01:15','',211,'http://localhost:8090/?p=214',0,'revision','',0),(215,0,'2025-12-17 12:31:54','2025-12-17 12:31:54','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25554\" class=\"elementor elementor-25554\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1978, Rasht, Iran and lives in Tehran</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>001 B.A in Painting / Graduated from Art and Architecture College, Tehran</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2012 Toy Story, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Nagayamon Art Gallery,Tsukuba,Japan.<br />2010 “The Cold Sore” X V A Gallery,Dubai.<br />2010 “Song of Black Tulips” Calo bookshop and cafe (Osaka) Japan.<br />2010 Art De Art View Gallery,Osaka,Japan.<br />2010 “Cold Sore” Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2008 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2007 Fukka Art Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2006 Tribal Art B8 Gallery,Fukuoka,Japan.<br />2005 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2004 Day Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2004 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2003 Laleh Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-07ccc67 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"07ccc67\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f1bd0c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6f1bd0c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2011 Morono Kiang Gallery.Los Angeles. U.S.A.<br />2011 International Book Festival of Illustrated books” 23-28 of May at La Central del Raval bookstore, Barcelona. Spain.<br />2011 “Festival little circus Flying circus Cagliari” 13-15 may Cultural Centre Exmà CAGLIARI(SARDINIA) Italy.<br />2011 “The first exhibition of Iranian illustrators” 14 May – 4 June in Neurotitan Gallery, Berlin, Germany.<br />2011 “My Super Hero” Morano Kiang Gallery Los Angeles,USA.<br />2011 “My Super Hero” Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2011 “Doll” Shirin Art Gallery, Group Exhibition.Tehran,Iran.<br />2011 “Between the Line” XVA Gallery,Dubai.<br />2010 Cream Art Gallery. Milan Italy.<br />2010 “The beat of young Iranian contemporary art”Ministry of Nomads,London.<br />2010 “Pagineacolori in Viaggio” Festival, (Tarquinia) Italy.<br />2010 “Song of Persia” LOGOS GALLERY, (TOKYO, SHIBUYA) Japan.<br />2010 Aurum Glory Art Space in Taipei,Taiwan.<br />2010 “The Story Teller” Taiwan New Arts Union in Tainan,Taiwan.<br />2010 “Oggi Me Ne Vado,Resto a Teheran” Cream-art Gallery,Milan,Italy.<br />2009 Works on paper from the “LAAL” collection,Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2008 Radical Drawing,Tehran Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2006 “7 auf einen streich” Geschaftsfuhrer Designaustria,Wien,Austria.<br />2006 Museo Civicodi Storia Naturale Giacomo Doria,Modena,Italy.<br />2005 “ARTEDEN” Art Center, Trieste, Italy.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae34108 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"ae34108\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Art Fairs and Other				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c320d0b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c320d0b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2010 Magic of Persia Contemporary Art Prize, Dubai (selected shortlist)<br />2010 Art Dubai – Contemporary Art fair. Dubai.<br />2010 Roma Contemporary Art Fair, Italy.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3de662 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"c3de662\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Press				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ed8445a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ed8445a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2010 Article for exhibition “Childish Strokes of genius” By: Jyoti Kalsi, 10 December, Dubai.<br />2010 Studio fludd No. 1 ,Interview. December, Italy.<br />2010 Notpaper, a blog dedicated to showcasing the work of international collage artists, Interview , Canada.<br />2009 Tandis Art Biweekly Magazine No.162, Interview, November, Tehran.<br />2009 Tandis Art Biweekly Magazine No.163, Amir Soghrati, November,Tehran.<br />2007 Shargh Newspaper, Interview, July,Tehran.<br />2006 Article for book ” Where are you going Aunt Cockroach?” by Gomi Taro Japan.<br />2006 llustration Magazine No.162,promote and interview ,Japan.<br />2006 1000 Und 1 Inhalt Magazine ” Das Magazin Fur Kinder-Und Jugendliteratur ” No.1,February, Austria.<br />2006 Varoom Magazine No.2,the Journal of illustration and made images, Uk.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d9742d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4d9742d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Training Experiences				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-91d9f41 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"91d9f41\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2011 Management of a 3-day workshop at the Emad studio, Lahijan. Iran.<br />2010 Management of a 3-day workshop at the Maazyar Elmi-Karbordi University, Mazandaran. Iran.<br />2009 Management of a 1-day workshop at the House of Iranian Artists, Tehran . Iran.<br />2007 Establishment of Kveta Studio and professional training of illustration Tehran. Iran.<br />2006 Management of a 2-day workshop along with Linda Wolfsgruber, Cultural Complex of Jahad Daneshgahi, Mashad. Iran.<br />2006 Management of a 3-day workshop in Sarmede, Italy.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d45351 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4d45351\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Prizes				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6964369 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6964369\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2009 Selected Artist and winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book fair, Italy<br />2009 C.J picture Book Festival, 2nd Prize, South Korea.<br />2008 Honor Diploma from International Board on Books for young People (IBBY) for “Goodnight commander”, Copenhagen, Denmark.<br />2008 Honor Diploma from the International Board on Books for Young People (IBBY), Norway and international Announcement of the Book, “Goodnight Commander”.<br />2008 Teatrio Exhibition, Third Prize for Book making, Venice, Italy.<br />2007 Honor Diploma from 3rd Barriero Biennial, Portugal<br />2006 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book fair, Italy.<br />2006 Noma Illustration Concours, Japan, Encouragment Prize.<br />2005 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book Fair, Italy.<br />2003 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book Fair, Italy<br />2003 42nd Belgrade Exhibition of Illustration, Winner of Golden Pen and Second Prize.<br />2002 5th Tehran Biennial of Illustration, Second Prize (T.I.B.I)</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8588af0 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"8588af0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Contests				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-df7e02f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"df7e02f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2010 Cream – art Gallery, Milan, Italy<br />2009 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna, Italy.<br />2009 C.J picture Book Festival, Seoul, Korea.<br />2009 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2008 C.J picture Book Festival, Seoul, Korea.<br />2008 “One thousand and one Nights” Contemporary Children’s Book Illustration from Iran, Barreiro, Portugal.<br />2008 ” Ghosts And Get Aways” Teatrio festival, Venice, Italy.<br />2007 “Playpen” New Children’s Book Illustration (Laurence King Publishing) London, UK.<br />2007 “Outstanding Books for Young People Disabilities” Norway.<br />2007 “Theatre de villeneuve les Maguelone” paris, France.<br />2007 Biennale International Exhibition of Children’s Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2006 “Bille Der Far Iran” Copenhagen,Denmark.<br />2006 “Noma” The Prize Winning Works Of The 15Th Concours for picture Book illustrations, Tokyo, Japan.<br />2006 “The First International Illustration Exhibition Of Dictionaries Book, Tehran, Iran.<br />2006 First Croatian Biennial Of Illustration, Zagreb.<br />2006 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna,Italy.<br />2005 Biennale International Exhibition of Children’s Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2005 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna, Italy.<br />2005 ” The 43rd golden pen of Belgrade” Progres Gallery, Serbia<br />2004 “Le Immagini della fantasia” sarmede, Italy.<br />2003 Biennal International Exhibition of Childrens Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2003 ” The 43rd golden pen of Belgrade” Progres Gallery, Serbia.<br />2003 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2003 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna,Italy.<br />2001 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2001 “5th Tehran Biennale Of Illustration [T.I.B.I] Tehran, Iran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3cb7e11 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3cb7e11\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Other Activities				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-91cc0ec elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"91cc0ec\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2009 Participation in the International Peace Day workshop, spring, Tehran.<br />2008 Speech regarding the significance of fabricating and processing of a graphic work, Khatam Al Anbia Complex, Rasht,.<br />2008 Speech regarding status of illustration, Ghom.<br />2008 Speech regarding significance of illustration drawing, Mirmiran Gallery, House of Iranian Artists Spring,Tehran.<br />2007 Participating in a 3-day workshop, supervised by Partic Benson, Tehran.<br />2007 Member of board of founders and jurors of Lak Lak Group in the International Exhibition of Dictionaries, Tehran.<br />2006 Speech regarding illustration, Iranian Children &amp; Youth’s Book Review &amp; Information Journal.<br />2006 Participating in a 3-mounth workshop supervised by Linda Wolfsgruber, Tehran.<br />2005 Participating in a 1-week workshop at Artedon Art Center, Italy.<br />2004 Speech regarding illustration, Iranian Children &amp; Adult Youth’s Book Review &amp; Information Journal.<br />2003 Participating in a 3-day workshop supervised by Shijio Nishimora, Tehran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7edee40 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"7edee40\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-eb6e244 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"eb6e244\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h4>Morteza Zahedi</h4></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\"> </div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h3>Toy Story</h3><p>19 March – 30 April 2012</p><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>XVA Gallery welcomes the return of Iranian artist Morteza Zahedi for his upcoming solo exhibition ‘Toy Story’, opening March 19th at XVA Gallery, DIFC and on display until April 30th. This new body of work comprises a large number of pieces created in a variety of medium – works on paper, bronzes and installation; including neon and found objects</p><p>“Morteza Zahedi is a unique creator, a creator who travels between apparently opposing universes.</p><p>Travelling through Morteza’s work is like travelling through an exotic garden full of shapes, colours and sensations, reminding us faintly of the remote territories of childhood and at the same time surprising us at every step with unknown and evocative stimuli.</p><p>Morteza, without making value judgements, uses the plasticity of hand to hand combat, of the beauty of confrontation, the seduction of conflict, to show the hidden face of both combatants and unover their virtues and flaws. There are no good guys and bad guys, no winners and losers; what we find is a complex and multifarious universe of attitudes and perceptions which is shown in the expressive tension of each piece, in each assemblage, in each of these new toys which no longer serve the game for which they were created, and now serve interpretation and analysis.”</p><p><strong>Isidro Ferrer, February 2012</strong></p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-61c0a9b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"61c0a9b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h4>Morteza Zahedi</h4></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\"> </div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h3>The Cold Sore</h3><p>28 November – 5 January 2011</p></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\">Once the crowded and dispersed characteristic of Tehran is intermingled with the joyful and lively nature of Guilan, what emerges, is a person named Morteza Zahedi whose artworks are complete carbon copies of his joyful mind. Zahedi is by nature a painter, whether in his compositional conduct, or his fluctuating manner of speech, or even in his on and off expressions of feelings. Whether he is painting or when he is making boxes; with the first glance, we understand that his mind, like that of Turner, even in its tranquility is in turmoil; and of course this turmoil has no connection to that of Turner. In any case, Zahedi cherishes this turmoil and explodes it in improvisations that flavor his brown-papers with the taste of watermelon.</div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>His papers, once full of lines and things, are reminiscent of the grandmothers’ pantries, with the same precision, experience and delicacies for ordering things within the frames.</p><p><strong>Vahid Sharifian, winter of 2010</strong></p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Morteza Zahedi','<p>Bio Born in 1978, Rasht, Iran and lives in Tehran Education 001 B.A in Painting / Graduated from Art and Architecture College, Tehran Selected Solo Exhibitions 2012 Toy Story, XVA Gallery, Dubai2011 Nagayamon Art Gallery,Tsukuba,Japan.2010 “The Cold Sore” X V A Gallery,Dubai.2010 “Song of Black Tulips” Calo bookshop and cafe (Osaka) Japan.2010 Art De Art [&hellip;]</p>\n','publish','closed','closed','','morteza-zahedi','','','2026-08-21 05:48:58','2026-08-21 05:48:58','',0,'http://localhost:8090/artist/morteza-zahedi/',0,'xva_artist','',0),(216,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:17','2026-08-20 21:01:17','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25554\" class=\"elementor elementor-25554\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1978, Rasht, Iran and lives in Tehran</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>001 B.A in Painting / Graduated from Art and Architecture College, Tehran</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2012 Toy Story, XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 Nagayamon Art Gallery,Tsukuba,Japan.<br />2010 “The Cold Sore” X V A Gallery,Dubai.<br />2010 “Song of Black Tulips” Calo bookshop and cafe (Osaka) Japan.<br />2010 Art De Art View Gallery,Osaka,Japan.<br />2010 “Cold Sore” Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2008 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2007 Fukka Art Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2006 Tribal Art B8 Gallery,Fukuoka,Japan.<br />2005 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2004 Day Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2004 T.Box Gallery,Tokyo,Japan.<br />2003 Laleh Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-07ccc67 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"07ccc67\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f1bd0c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6f1bd0c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2011 Morono Kiang Gallery.Los Angeles. U.S.A.<br />2011 International Book Festival of Illustrated books” 23-28 of May at La Central del Raval bookstore, Barcelona. Spain.<br />2011 “Festival little circus Flying circus Cagliari” 13-15 may Cultural Centre Exmà CAGLIARI(SARDINIA) Italy.<br />2011 “The first exhibition of Iranian illustrators” 14 May – 4 June in Neurotitan Gallery, Berlin, Germany.<br />2011 “My Super Hero” Morano Kiang Gallery Los Angeles,USA.<br />2011 “My Super Hero” Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2011 “Doll” Shirin Art Gallery, Group Exhibition.Tehran,Iran.<br />2011 “Between the Line” XVA Gallery,Dubai.<br />2010 Cream Art Gallery. Milan Italy.<br />2010 “The beat of young Iranian contemporary art”Ministry of Nomads,London.<br />2010 “Pagineacolori in Viaggio” Festival, (Tarquinia) Italy.<br />2010 “Song of Persia” LOGOS GALLERY, (TOKYO, SHIBUYA) Japan.<br />2010 Aurum Glory Art Space in Taipei,Taiwan.<br />2010 “The Story Teller” Taiwan New Arts Union in Tainan,Taiwan.<br />2010 “Oggi Me Ne Vado,Resto a Teheran” Cream-art Gallery,Milan,Italy.<br />2009 Works on paper from the “LAAL” collection,Aaran Art Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2008 Radical Drawing,Tehran Gallery,Tehran,Iran.<br />2006 “7 auf einen streich” Geschaftsfuhrer Designaustria,Wien,Austria.<br />2006 Museo Civicodi Storia Naturale Giacomo Doria,Modena,Italy.<br />2005 “ARTEDEN” Art Center, Trieste, Italy.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae34108 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"ae34108\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Art Fairs and Other				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c320d0b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c320d0b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>2010 Magic of Persia Contemporary Art Prize, Dubai (selected shortlist)<br />2010 Art Dubai – Contemporary Art fair. Dubai.<br />2010 Roma Contemporary Art Fair, Italy.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3de662 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"c3de662\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Press				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ed8445a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ed8445a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2010 Article for exhibition “Childish Strokes of genius” By: Jyoti Kalsi, 10 December, Dubai.<br />2010 Studio fludd No. 1 ,Interview. December, Italy.<br />2010 Notpaper, a blog dedicated to showcasing the work of international collage artists, Interview , Canada.<br />2009 Tandis Art Biweekly Magazine No.162, Interview, November, Tehran.<br />2009 Tandis Art Biweekly Magazine No.163, Amir Soghrati, November,Tehran.<br />2007 Shargh Newspaper, Interview, July,Tehran.<br />2006 Article for book ” Where are you going Aunt Cockroach?” by Gomi Taro Japan.<br />2006 llustration Magazine No.162,promote and interview ,Japan.<br />2006 1000 Und 1 Inhalt Magazine ” Das Magazin Fur Kinder-Und Jugendliteratur ” No.1,February, Austria.<br />2006 Varoom Magazine No.2,the Journal of illustration and made images, Uk.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d9742d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4d9742d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Training Experiences				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-91d9f41 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"91d9f41\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2011 Management of a 3-day workshop at the Emad studio, Lahijan. Iran.<br />2010 Management of a 3-day workshop at the Maazyar Elmi-Karbordi University, Mazandaran. Iran.<br />2009 Management of a 1-day workshop at the House of Iranian Artists, Tehran . Iran.<br />2007 Establishment of Kveta Studio and professional training of illustration Tehran. Iran.<br />2006 Management of a 2-day workshop along with Linda Wolfsgruber, Cultural Complex of Jahad Daneshgahi, Mashad. Iran.<br />2006 Management of a 3-day workshop in Sarmede, Italy.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d45351 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"4d45351\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Prizes				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6964369 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6964369\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2009 Selected Artist and winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book fair, Italy<br />2009 C.J picture Book Festival, 2nd Prize, South Korea.<br />2008 Honor Diploma from International Board on Books for young People (IBBY) for “Goodnight commander”, Copenhagen, Denmark.<br />2008 Honor Diploma from the International Board on Books for Young People (IBBY), Norway and international Announcement of the Book, “Goodnight Commander”.<br />2008 Teatrio Exhibition, Third Prize for Book making, Venice, Italy.<br />2007 Honor Diploma from 3rd Barriero Biennial, Portugal<br />2006 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book fair, Italy.<br />2006 Noma Illustration Concours, Japan, Encouragment Prize.<br />2005 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book Fair, Italy.<br />2003 Selected Artist and Winner of Honor Diploma from Bologna Book Fair, Italy<br />2003 42nd Belgrade Exhibition of Illustration, Winner of Golden Pen and Second Prize.<br />2002 5th Tehran Biennial of Illustration, Second Prize (T.I.B.I)</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8588af0 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"8588af0\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Contests				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-df7e02f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"df7e02f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2010 Cream – art Gallery, Milan, Italy<br />2009 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna, Italy.<br />2009 C.J picture Book Festival, Seoul, Korea.<br />2009 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2008 C.J picture Book Festival, Seoul, Korea.<br />2008 “One thousand and one Nights” Contemporary Children’s Book Illustration from Iran, Barreiro, Portugal.<br />2008 ” Ghosts And Get Aways” Teatrio festival, Venice, Italy.<br />2007 “Playpen” New Children’s Book Illustration (Laurence King Publishing) London, UK.<br />2007 “Outstanding Books for Young People Disabilities” Norway.<br />2007 “Theatre de villeneuve les Maguelone” paris, France.<br />2007 Biennale International Exhibition of Children’s Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2006 “Bille Der Far Iran” Copenhagen,Denmark.<br />2006 “Noma” The Prize Winning Works Of The 15Th Concours for picture Book illustrations, Tokyo, Japan.<br />2006 “The First International Illustration Exhibition Of Dictionaries Book, Tehran, Iran.<br />2006 First Croatian Biennial Of Illustration, Zagreb.<br />2006 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna,Italy.<br />2005 Biennale International Exhibition of Children’s Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2005 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna, Italy.<br />2005 ” The 43rd golden pen of Belgrade” Progres Gallery, Serbia<br />2004 “Le Immagini della fantasia” sarmede, Italy.<br />2003 Biennal International Exhibition of Childrens Book Illustration, Barriero, Portugal.<br />2003 ” The 43rd golden pen of Belgrade” Progres Gallery, Serbia.<br />2003 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2003 Bologna Children’s Book Fair” Illustrators Annual ” Bologna,Italy.<br />2001 Biennale of Illustration Bratislava [BIB] Slovak Republic.<br />2001 “5th Tehran Biennale Of Illustration [T.I.B.I] Tehran, Iran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3cb7e11 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3cb7e11\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Other Activities				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-91cc0ec elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"91cc0ec\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2009 Participation in the International Peace Day workshop, spring, Tehran.<br />2008 Speech regarding the significance of fabricating and processing of a graphic work, Khatam Al Anbia Complex, Rasht,.<br />2008 Speech regarding status of illustration, Ghom.<br />2008 Speech regarding significance of illustration drawing, Mirmiran Gallery, House of Iranian Artists Spring,Tehran.<br />2007 Participating in a 3-day workshop, supervised by Partic Benson, Tehran.<br />2007 Member of board of founders and jurors of Lak Lak Group in the International Exhibition of Dictionaries, Tehran.<br />2006 Speech regarding illustration, Iranian Children &amp; Youth’s Book Review &amp; Information Journal.<br />2006 Participating in a 3-mounth workshop supervised by Linda Wolfsgruber, Tehran.<br />2005 Participating in a 1-week workshop at Artedon Art Center, Italy.<br />2004 Speech regarding illustration, Iranian Children &amp; Adult Youth’s Book Review &amp; Information Journal.<br />2003 Participating in a 3-day workshop supervised by Shijio Nishimora, Tehran.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7edee40 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"7edee40\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-eb6e244 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"eb6e244\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h4>Morteza Zahedi</h4></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\"> </div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h3>Toy Story</h3><p>19 March – 30 April 2012</p><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>XVA Gallery welcomes the return of Iranian artist Morteza Zahedi for his upcoming solo exhibition ‘Toy Story’, opening March 19th at XVA Gallery, DIFC and on display until April 30th. This new body of work comprises a large number of pieces created in a variety of medium – works on paper, bronzes and installation; including neon and found objects</p><p>“Morteza Zahedi is a unique creator, a creator who travels between apparently opposing universes.</p><p>Travelling through Morteza’s work is like travelling through an exotic garden full of shapes, colours and sensations, reminding us faintly of the remote territories of childhood and at the same time surprising us at every step with unknown and evocative stimuli.</p><p>Morteza, without making value judgements, uses the plasticity of hand to hand combat, of the beauty of confrontation, the seduction of conflict, to show the hidden face of both combatants and unover their virtues and flaws. There are no good guys and bad guys, no winners and losers; what we find is a complex and multifarious universe of attitudes and perceptions which is shown in the expressive tension of each piece, in each assemblage, in each of these new toys which no longer serve the game for which they were created, and now serve interpretation and analysis.”</p><p><strong>Isidro Ferrer, February 2012</strong></p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-61c0a9b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"61c0a9b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h4>Morteza Zahedi</h4></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\"> </div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><h3>The Cold Sore</h3><p>28 November – 5 January 2011</p></div></div><div class=\"vc_empty_space\">Once the crowded and dispersed characteristic of Tehran is intermingled with the joyful and lively nature of Guilan, what emerges, is a person named Morteza Zahedi whose artworks are complete carbon copies of his joyful mind. Zahedi is by nature a painter, whether in his compositional conduct, or his fluctuating manner of speech, or even in his on and off expressions of feelings. Whether he is painting or when he is making boxes; with the first glance, we understand that his mind, like that of Turner, even in its tranquility is in turmoil; and of course this turmoil has no connection to that of Turner. In any case, Zahedi cherishes this turmoil and explodes it in improvisations that flavor his brown-papers with the taste of watermelon.</div><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>His papers, once full of lines and things, are reminiscent of the grandmothers’ pantries, with the same precision, experience and delicacies for ordering things within the frames.</p><p><strong>Vahid Sharifian, winter of 2010</strong></p></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Morteza Zahedi','<p>Bio Born in 1978, Rasht, Iran and lives in Tehran Education 001 B.A in Painting / Graduated from Art and Architecture College, Tehran Selected Solo Exhibitions 2012 Toy Story, XVA Gallery, Dubai2011 Nagayamon Art Gallery,Tsukuba,Japan.2010 “The Cold Sore” X V A Gallery,Dubai.2010 “Song of Black Tulips” Calo bookshop and cafe (Osaka) Japan.2010 Art De Art [&hellip;]</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','215-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:17','2026-08-20 21:01:17','',215,'http://localhost:8090/?p=216',0,'revision','',0),(217,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:18','2026-08-20 21:01:18','','Morteza Zahedi','','inherit','open','closed','','morteza-zahedi-2','','','2026-08-20 21:01:18','2026-08-20 21:01:18','',215,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MZ-145-imageUntitled-3-2013-Woolen-157-x-90-x-52-cm.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(218,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:19','2026-08-20 21:01:19','','Morteza Zahedi','','inherit','open','closed','','morteza-zahedi-3','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MZ-145-imageUntitled-3-2013-Woolen-157-x-90-x-52-cm-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(219,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:20','2026-08-20 21:01:20','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25544\" class=\"elementor elementor-25544\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>B. 1945, D. 2022. Lived and worked between Beirut and Amman, where she was born. She studied sculpture at the École nationale supérieure des Beaux-Arts in Paris, France. Saudi sculpted mainly in stone. Her forms are full of vitality, beauty and a clear sense of equilibrium. Saudi created her first sculpture in stone in 1965, named Mother/Earth. She frequently returned to ideas of fertility and growth. Always starting with basic shapes: the square, circle, cylinder, rectangle, she goes on to give them movement, a life of their own by either repeating their forms, varying their depths or heights, or cutting them across one another to create new, graceful compositions. She described herself as a stone lover, respecting and manipulating the primary material of the earth to create her powerful and timeless works. Saudi revels in finding different forms of natural stone from the Middle East, using white marble from Carrara, pink limestone and green marble from Jordan, or black diorite from Syria, Mona creates modern, abstract forms expressing themes of life force and creation. A monumental sculpture by Mona Saudi stands outside the Institut du Monde Arabe in Paris, the only work permitted to grace the surrounding precinct by its architect Jean Nouvel.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>École Nationale Supérieure des Beaux-Arts, Paris, France.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2018 Retrospective Exhibition, Sharjah Art Museum, UAE.<br />2017 Saleh Barakat Gallery, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />2015 Poetry in Stone, Lawrie Shabibi, Dubai, UAE.<br />2013 Joint exhibition with daughter Dia Batal, Jacaranda Images Gallery, Amman, Jordan.<br />2012 Artcircle Gallery, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />2011 Saint John Perse Foundation, Aix-en-Provence, France.<br />2011 Europia Gallery, Paris, France.<br />2010 Jacaranda Images Gallery, Amman, Jordan.<br />2010 The Mosaic Rooms, AM Qattan Foundation, London, UK.<br />2004 Quartier des Arts, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1999 Al‐Oudaya Museum, Rabat, Morocco.<br />1995 Retrospective, Darat Al-Funun, Amman, Jordan.<br />1992 Galerie 50 x 70, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1985 Al-Salmiyah Gallery, Kuwait.<br />1984 Alif Gallery, Washington D.C., WA, USA.<br />1983 Alia Gallery, Amman, Jordan.<br />1982 Galerie Epreuve d’Artiste, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1981 Galerie Elissar, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1975 Galerie Contemporaine, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1973 Galerie One, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1971 Galerie Vercamer, Paris, France.<br />1963 Café de la Presse, Beirut, Lebanon.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-07ccc67 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"07ccc67\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f1bd0c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6f1bd0c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2018 Abu Dhabi Art, with Lawrie Shabibi, Abu Dhabi, UAE.<br />2016 Abu Dhabi Art, with Lawrie Shabibi, Abu Dhabi, UAE.<br />2015 Art Dubai Contemporary, with Lawrie Shabibi, Dubai, UAE.<br />2014 Abu Dhabi Art, with Lawrie Shabibi, Abu Dhabi, UAE.<br />2012 Le Corps Découvert, Institut du Monde Arabe, Paris, France.<br />2003 International Cairo Biennale, Cairo, Egypt.<br />2001 Les Ateliers Arabes, UNESCO, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1997 Voyage en Jordanie, Hotel de Ville, Paris, France.<br />1996 Rhythm and Form, Visual Reflections on Poetry, USA.<br />1994 Forces of Change, National Museum of Women in the Arts, Washington D.C., WA, USA.<br />1993 – 2011 Salon d’Automne, Sursok Museum, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1987 Arab Contemporary Artists, Institut du Monde Arabe, Paris, France.<br />1981 Arab Artists, Kunst Hus, Oslo, Norway.<br />1979 Palestinian Art, Oriental Museum, Moscow, Russia.<br />1978 International Art Exhibition for Palestine, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />1978 Colamarini and his Students, Musee Rodin, Paris, France.<br />1972 – 1973 Salon de Mai, Musee d’Art Moderne, Paris, France.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae34108 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"ae34108\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Public and Private Collections				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c320d0b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c320d0b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Sharjah Art Foundation, Sharjah, UAE.<br />The British Museum, London, UK.<br />Barjeel Art Foundation, Sharjah, UAE.<br />Institut du Monde Arabe, Paris, France.<br />National Museum for Women in the Arts, Washington D.C., WA, USA.<br />Dar Al Athar Al Islamiyya, Kuwait Museum of Modern Art, Kuwait.<br />National Gallery of the Fine Arts, Amman, Jordan.<br />The Khaled Shoman Foundation, Amman, Jordan.<br />Sursock Museum, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />Assila Museum, Morocco.<br />French Embassy, Amman, Jordan.<br />Arab Bank Headquarters, Amman, Jordan.<br />Cairo Bank Headquarters, Amman, Jordan.<br />Jabal Amman, Public Square, Amman, Jordan.<br />University of Science &amp; Technology, Irbid, Jordan.<br />Al Wafa Bank, Casablanca, Morocco.<br />International Sculpture Park, Rashana, Lebanon.<br />Al Hariri Art Collection, Beirut, Lebanon.<br />Ministry of Culture, Cairo, Egypt.</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3de662 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"c3de662\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Publications				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ed8445a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ed8445a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2012 Hommage a Mahmoud Darwish.<br />2011 Hommage a Saint John Perse, drawings for ‘Chant pour an Equinoxe’.<br />2011 Petra Tablets, drawings for a poem by Adonis, Arabic &amp; English.<br />2006 Forty Years in Sculpture, monograph showing works created between 1965 and 2005, Arabic, English and French.<br />1995 Le Bourgeonnement du Désert, sculptures and poem by Michel Butor.<br />1992 An Ocean of Dreams, poetry and drawings.<br />1972 First Vision, poetry and drawings.<br />1970 In Time of War: Children Testify.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Mona Saudi','<p>Bio B. 1945, D. 2022. Lived and worked between Beirut and Amman, where she was born. She studied sculpture at the École nationale supérieure des Beaux-Arts in Paris, France. Saudi sculpted mainly in stone. Her forms are full of vitality, beauty and a clear sense of equilibrium. Saudi created her first sculpture in stone in [&hellip;]</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','70-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:20','2026-08-20 21:01:20','',70,'http://localhost:8090/?p=219',0,'revision','',0),(220,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:22','2026-08-20 21:01:22','','Mona Saudi','','inherit','open','closed','','mona-saudi-5','','','2026-08-20 21:01:22','2026-08-20 21:01:22','',70,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MNS-010-imageHommage-a-Saint-John-Perse-2007-Signed-dated-Silk-Screen-Print-49-x-34-cm-33-77.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(221,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:23','2026-08-20 21:01:23','','Mona Saudi','','inherit','open','closed','','mona-saudi-6','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MNS-010-imageHommage-a-Saint-John-Perse-2007-Signed-dated-Silk-Screen-Print-49-x-34-cm-33-77-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(222,0,'2025-12-17 12:23:11','2025-12-17 12:23:11','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25535\" class=\"elementor elementor-25535\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6141c2d elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6141c2d\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in 1958 Iran, lives in New York</p><p>Mahmoud Hamadani’s works have been shown at The British Museum, The New Museum of Contemporary Art in New York, as well as numerous solo and group exhibitions in New York, London, Dubai, Lausanne, Beirut and Hong Kong. He is in the permanent collections of The Metropolitan Museum of Art and The British Museum. He is a recipient of Pollock-Krasner Foundation grant.</p><p>Hamadani earned a BA in Mathematics from State University of New York and a Masters degree in Public Administration from the Kennedy School of Government at Harvard University.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1992 John F. Kennedy School of Government, Harvard University – Master in Public Administration<br />1981 State University of New York, BA in Mathematics</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Solo Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4a86dd6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4a86dd6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2024 XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2023 Art on 56th, Beirut<br />2017 DubnerModerne,Lausanne,Switzerland<br />2016 Adelphi University, New York.<br />2015 Shirin Gallery, New York<br />2009 XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2009 Michael Steinberg Fine Art, New York<br />2006 7 Bedford Row, London<br />2004 Michael Steinberg Fine Art, New York<br />1999 Karen McCready Fine Art, New York</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-07ccc67 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"07ccc67\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Group Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f1bd0c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6f1bd0c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2023 MENART FAIR, Paris<br />2023 XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2023 Bienvenu, Steinberg &amp; J, New York<br />2022 MENART FAIR, Paris<br />2021 KristenLorelloGallery,NewYork<br />2019 Susan Eley Fine Art, New York;<br />2019 Hammond Museum, North Salem, NY;<br />2019Art New York, Marc Hachem Gallery<br />2018 Scope Art Fair, New York<br />2018 Mana Contemporary, Jersey City, NJ<br />2017 De Buck Gallery, New York<br />2016 XVA Gallery, Dubai. Shirin Gallery, New York.<br />2015 Art Hamptons Art Fair, New York Shirin Gallery, New York<br />2014 Singapore Art fair Abu Dhabi Art fair<br />2013 De Buck Gallery, New York<br />2011 FORD PROJECT, New York<br />2011 XVA Gallery, Dubai<br />2011 New York University, Abu Dhabi<br />2009 Hong Kong International Art Fair<br />2009 Bastakiya Art fair, Dubai<br />2008 Dubai International Finance Center, Dubai<br />2006 The British Museum, London<br />2003 University Gallery, University of Florida, Gainesville<br />Korea Gallery, New York<br />New York University Small Works Exhibition<br />2002 The Work Space, New York<br />New York University Small Works Exhibition<br />2001 New Museum of Contemporary Art, New York<br />2000 Percy-Miller Gallery, London<br />New York University Small Works Exhibition</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae34108 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"ae34108\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__te