antly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','68-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:43','2026-08-20 21:01:43','',68,'http://localhost:8090/?p=242',0,'revision','',0),(243,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:44','2026-08-20 21:01:44','','Hussein Al-Mohasen','','inherit','open','closed','','hussein-al-mohasen-5-2','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/HAM-72-imageThe-Color-Tank-2012-Graffiti-on-wood-101-x-210-cm.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(244,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:44','2026-08-20 21:01:44','','Hussein Al-Mohasen','','inherit','open','closed','','hussein-al-mohasen-5','','','2026-08-20 21:01:44','2026-08-20 21:01:44','',68,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/HAM-72-imageThe-Color-Tank-2012-Graffiti-on-wood-101-x-210-cm-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(245,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:46','2026-08-20 21:01:46','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25437\" class=\"elementor elementor-25437\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them. Interchangeably, sufi teachings are generally identified as highly individualistic and harmonious practices while being on the contrary- Observing the sporadic existence of dervish from the rise of sufism centuries ago,having being taken a vow of selfless love and distancing from the norms of society, they were and until now are deemed as controversial figures. Their presence brings uneasiness in social settings and questions the elaborate ways of the tediously complicated belief system. Similar to the silent uneasiness I try to achieve through my practice. </p><p>Manifesting creatures like bees, birds and fish as symbols for their inter-religious references, geo-location and life cycle. Ornate and complex geometric drawings hailing from centuries of tradition of being adorned with natural pigments and organic materials, whilst I choose to treat them with fluorescent colors that are industrially made and artificial in nature implying towards the need of beliefs becoming more synthetic and fabricated rather than being the innate desire to be spiritual and organic. Consistently moving between these ideas the imagery stands as a metaphor and holds a multitude of meaning. Actions like shredding and restructuring pages from history books, reducing words from letters to dots (nuqta). Coming forth as a process of unlearning a plethora of information being fed over a period of time. In totality my practice melts down to a consistent effort in breaking down or simplifying the complexity of fabricated information into the importance of one single entity. One minimal existence that contains all.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>BFA National College of Arts Lahore Pakistan</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2024- Art as process at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2024- Fronde Sance at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2023- What the land knows the hearts remember, four person at ArtSoch Gallery, Lahore, Pakistan<br />2023- Neon Equilibrium Virtual NFTs Morrow Collective 2022- Made in Tashkeel 22, Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Into the revolution, at Foundry downtown<br />Dubai. curated by Morrow collective<br />2021- Solstice at XVA gallery, Dubai UAE<br />2021- Made in Tashkeel 2021, at Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Genesis online NFT show curated by Morrow collective UAE<br />2021- Silent Confabulations, solo show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is at Alliance Francaise Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is part1 at Beit funn Dubai sustainable city, Dubai UAE<br />2020- Wolf tone at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2019- Made in Tashkeel 2019 at Tashkeel Dubai,UAE<br />2018- Made-in Tashkeel 2018 At Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2013- The Bear Show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Huma Shoaib','<p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','26-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:46','2026-08-20 21:01:46','',26,'http://localhost:8090/?p=245',0,'revision','',0),(246,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:46','2026-08-20 21:01:46','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25437\" class=\"elementor elementor-25437\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them. Interchangeably, sufi teachings are generally identified as highly individualistic and harmonious practices while being on the contrary- Observing the sporadic existence of dervish from the rise of sufism centuries ago,having being taken a vow of selfless love and distancing from the norms of society, they were and until now are deemed as controversial figures. Their presence brings uneasiness in social settings and questions the elaborate ways of the tediously complicated belief system. Similar to the silent uneasiness I try to achieve through my practice. </p><p>Manifesting creatures like bees, birds and fish as symbols for their inter-religious references, geo-location and life cycle. Ornate and complex geometric drawings hailing from centuries of tradition of being adorned with natural pigments and organic materials, whilst I choose to treat them with fluorescent colors that are industrially made and artificial in nature implying towards the need of beliefs becoming more synthetic and fabricated rather than being the innate desire to be spiritual and organic. Consistently moving between these ideas the imagery stands as a metaphor and holds a multitude of meaning. Actions like shredding and restructuring pages from history books, reducing words from letters to dots (nuqta). Coming forth as a process of unlearning a plethora of information being fed over a period of time. In totality my practice melts down to a consistent effort in breaking down or simplifying the complexity of fabricated information into the importance of one single entity. One minimal existence that contains all.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>BFA National College of Arts Lahore Pakistan</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>2024- Art as process at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2024- Fronde Sance at XVA gallery Dubai, UAE<br />2023- What the land knows the hearts remember, four person at ArtSoch Gallery, Lahore, Pakistan<br />2023- Neon Equilibrium Virtual NFTs Morrow Collective 2022- Made in Tashkeel 22, Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Into the revolution, at Foundry downtown<br />Dubai. curated by Morrow collective<br />2021- Solstice at XVA gallery, Dubai UAE<br />2021- Made in Tashkeel 2021, at Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2021- Genesis online NFT show curated by Morrow collective UAE<br />2021- Silent Confabulations, solo show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is at Alliance Francaise Dubai UAE<br />2021- The world is too much with is part1 at Beit funn Dubai sustainable city, Dubai UAE<br />2020- Wolf tone at XVA gallery Dubai UAE<br />2019- Made in Tashkeel 2019 at Tashkeel Dubai,UAE<br />2018- Made-in Tashkeel 2018 At Tashkeel Dubai, UAE<br />2013- The Bear Show at XVA gallery Dubai UAE</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Huma Shoaib','<p>Significantly influenced by sufi ideologies, my work visually rests as serene and meditative in parallel to the disturbing questions of division and social hierarchy arising from them.</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','26-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:01:46','2026-08-20 21:01:46','',26,'http://localhost:8090/?p=246',0,'revision','',0),(247,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:47','2026-08-20 21:01:47','','Huma Shoaib','','inherit','open','closed','','huma-shoaib-5','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/HMS-015-imageconfabulations-1-2021-paper-cut-drawing-60x60cm.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(248,0,'2026-08-20 21:01:47','2026-08-20 21:01:47','','Huma Shoaib','','inherit','open','closed','','huma-shoaib-6','','','2026-08-20 21:01:47','2026-08-20 21:01:47','',26,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/HMS-015-imageconfabulations-1-2021-paper-cut-drawing-60x60cm-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(249,0,'2025-12-17 11:23:11','2025-12-17 11:23:11','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25429\" class=\"elementor elementor-25429\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d912eb9 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"d912eb9\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Bio				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29b2d23 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"29b2d23\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>Born in Austin, Texas to German parents; moved to Munich, Germany, at 8 years of age. Lives in Bed-Stuy, Brooklyn. Halona makes objects. Her work has been included in group and solo shows in Europe, the U.A.E. and New York. Halona co-founded Full Tank, an all-female experimental band with all original songs; her current band is Fetzig, also a DIY band.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-49f7abd elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"49f7abd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c8168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c3c8168\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>1990 – 1995 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Hochschule der Bildenden Kuenste Saar, Saarbruecken, Germany<br />1994 Studied Painting and Performance Art at the Nova Scotia College of Art and Design, Halifax, Canada</p>								</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-77ec13a elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"77ec13a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Selected Exhibitions				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1aabda4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1aabda4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>021 Halona Hilbertz: Fledgling Beasts, Sala Projects, New York, NY<br />2021 Sommerausstellung, Museum St. Wendel, Sankt Wendel, Germany<br />2020 Uncertainty, Viridian Artists Gallery, New York, NY<br />2019 Empathetic Dream Construction: Braithwaite, Hilbertz &amp; Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2018 The Doll Show, Ceres Gallery, New York, NY<br />2018 Small Works, Trestle Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2017 Europe in China: Contemporary Sculpture Exhibition from Germany, Austria and Switzerland, Qingdao Sculpture Museum, Qingdao, China<br />2017 Collectivity: Objects and Associations in the U.A.E. Art World, Maraya Art Centre, Sharjah, United Arab Emirates<br />2017 Culture of One, sTudio 7 Gallery, Fort Tilden, NY<br />2015 Dog, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2014 Curiouser and Curiouser: Halona Hilbertz, Colleen Quigley &amp; Jakob Roepke, XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2013 13th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2012 12th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2011 Rendezvous: Exposition Internationale d’Art Contemporain en Region du Val de Loire (Catalogue) Domaine Saint Hilaire, Roiffe, France<br />2010 Creative Couples, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2010 11th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2009 10th Annual Williamsburg Salon Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2008 Katja Fratzscher &amp; Halona Hilbertz: Zeichnungen &amp; Objekte, 2-person show, curated by Anna Schädlich, Q-Club, Berlin, Germany<br />2008 9th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Play, Proteus Gowanus, Brooklyn, NY<br />2007 Wish You Were Here, A.I.R. Gallery, New York, NY<br />2007 20 Birds (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2006 Laundry-Women-Art, Bliss Street Studio Gallery, Queens, NY<br />2006 Halona Hilbertz: Wall Dolls. Donn Davis: Collage Paintings. (Two Person Show) XVA Gallery, Dubai, United Arab Emirates<br />2006 Terrible Toy Fair III CBGB Art Gallery, New York, NY<br />2006 Cyclical States of Boredom in the Face of World Domination Rachel Mason’s Studio, Brooklyn, NY<br />2005 Pfiennale Pfiff Restaurant, New York, NY<br />2005 8th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 Dollhouses in the Dollhaus Gallery, Brooklyn, NY<br />2004 P.M.S./Women Painters, Musicians and Sculptors, Brooklyn College Art Gallery at the Brooklyn War Memorial, NY<br />2004 7th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 Dollops, Knit Objects &amp; Wall Dolls (Solo), Amarin Thai Cafe, Brooklyn, NY<br />2003 WACO Show 49 Ann, New York, NY<br />2003 New Art Show Hines Studios, Charleston, SC<br />2003 Everything Must Go (27-Artist Show, Co-Curated with Donn Davis, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, New York<br />2003 6th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY\\<br />2002 5th Annual Williamsburg Salon, Williamsburg Art &amp; Historical Center, Brooklyn, NY<br />2001 Williamsburg Arts and Culture Festival, 59 Harrison Avenue, Brooklyn, NY<br />2000 Elsewhe