n Jose Institute of Contemporary Art, California, USA.<br />2016: Surface and Subtext, Everard Read Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2016: -nano Barnard Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2016/2015: Map of the New Art – Imago Mundi – Luciano Benetton Collection, Isola di San Giorgio Maggiore, Venezia, Italy and New York, USA.<br />2016: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2016: Lush, SMAC Gallery, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2015: Ten years of Artists Books, A collection of artists’ books curated for the Brooklyn Public Library, New York, USA.<br />2015: Homage, Everard Read, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2015: Picture &amp; Paper, Barnard Gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2015: The Spiritual in the Material, Lizamore and Associates Gallery, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2015: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2015: The Artist as Author, Klein Karoo Nasionale Kunstefees, Oudshoorn, South Africa.<br />2015: Empire, Everard Read, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2014: Butterflies in my Stomach, XVA Gallery, Al Fahidi, Dubai, UAE.<br />2014: Capital: Contemporary, Fried Contemporary, Pretoria, South Africa.<br />2014: The Art of the Book, The Seager Gray Gallery, San Francisco, USA.<br />2013: Crossing the Divide Erdmann Contemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2013: Wonder Works, The Space, Hong Kong, HK.<br />2012: Conversations, Sydney, Australia.<br />2012: Clover Aardklop Arts Festival, Potcheftstroom, South Africa.<br />2011: Implemented Environments, Brundyn &amp; Gonsalves, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Conceptual Matters (part II), ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: The Mysteries and Mechanics of Perception, iArt, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Es(Cape), Pretoria Kunsvereniging, Pretoria, South Africa.<br />2010: Return to the Land, Klein Karoo Kunstefees, Oudshoorn, South Africa.<br />2010: Matters Conceptually(part I), ErdmannContemporary, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2010: Reading between the lines, US Gallery, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2009: 3d Riwaq Biennale, Birzeit, Palestine.<br />2008-2009: Construct: Beyond the Documentary Photograph (Travelling exhibition) Unisa Gallery, Pretoria, KZN Gallery, Durban, Nelson Mandela Metropolitan Gallery, Port Elizabeth, Grahamstown Art Festival (Main show), Grahamstown, Goethe Institute, Johannesburg, South Africa.<br />2008: Print 08: Myth, Memory and the Archive, Bell-Roberts Gallery, Woodstock, South Africa.<br />2007: Greenhouse, Bell-Roberts Gallery, Lourensford estate, Stellenbosch, South Africa.<br />2007: Critic and Committee’s Choice, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2007: Come, Michaelis Gallery, Cape Town, KZNSA, Durban, South Africa.<br />2007: Fest, Durbanville Cultural Centre, Durbanville, South Africa.<br />2005: Absolut Finale, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2005: FINDING YOU (Collaborative exhibition of ceramic installation), AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2004: Absolut Moment, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2004: Exfoliate (A collaborative printmaking exhibition), ArtB, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2003: Trilogy, Sanlam Gallery, ArtB, Durbanville Cultural Centre, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2003: Old and New (Selected old and new works from the Sanlam Collection), Sanlam gallery, Cape Town, South Africa.<br />2002: Absolut Voyeur, AVA, Cape Town, South Africa.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		','Barbara Wildenboer','<p>BIO Born in 1973, South Africa Barbara Wildenboer was born in Pretoria, South Africa in 1973. She received her Bachelor of Visual Arts from UNISA and completed her Masters in Fine Art (with distinction) at the Michaelis School of Art at the University of Cape Town in 2007. She currently lives and works in Cape [&hellip;]</p>\n','inherit','closed','closed','','61-revision-v1','','','2026-08-20 21:02:25','2026-08-20 21:02:25','',61,'http://localhost:8090/?p=273',0,'revision','',0),(274,0,'2026-08-20 21:02:27','2026-08-20 21:02:27','','Barbara Wildenboer','','inherit','open','closed','','barbara-wildenboer-5','','','2026-08-21 05:52:12','2026-08-21 05:52:12','',486,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/BBW-10-imageChaos-Theory-2020-Altered-Book.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(275,0,'2026-08-20 21:02:27','2026-08-20 21:02:27','','Barbara Wildenboer','','inherit','open','closed','','barbara-wildenboer-6','','','2026-08-20 21:02:27','2026-08-20 21:02:27','',61,'http://localhost:8090/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/BBW-10-imageChaos-Theory-2020-Altered-Book-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(276,0,'2026-08-20 21:02:29','2026-08-20 21:02:29','		<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"25294\" class=\"elementor elementor-25294\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f8c0087 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f8c0087\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2dd6d19 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"2dd6d19\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a16d54e elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"a16d54e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				BIO				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-95b3223 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"95b3223\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<p>Born in Erbil, Kurdistan – Iraq. Lives in Florence, Italy.</p><p>An international artist and a citizen of the world, Azad Nanakeli has focused his visual pattern on a multi-layered artistic discourse, at the crossroads between an impressive variety of media: painting, photography, video, installation, and an equally powerful narrative, which gives all his work an almost spiritual touch of coherence and unity. Born in Erbil, today part of the Kurdistan Autonomous Region in Iraq, currently living in Florence, Italy, Azad illustrated his trans-national mix of identity in around a hundred of international exhibitions, culminating in three editions of the Venice Biennale: the Kurdish pavilion in 2009, the Iraqi pavilion in 2011 and the Iranian pavilion in 2015.</p><p>Highlighted Memory, his solo exhibition in Dubai, was an invitation to an overview of Nanakeli’s major topics of reflection and a highly representative illustration of his innovative technique based on the overlapping of narrative and mixed media layers. The exhibition proposed a new frame where the artist could freely develop his own timeless connections between personal and trans-individual experiences, between the past and the present, between memory and identity. In Nanakeli’s view, art becomes a recording and a critical process, able to contribute to a comprehension of the social role and the meaning of the artistic practice, proposing a series of reflections on how much art can contribute to the configuration of the modern world representation; interrogating itself at the same time on how the artist can make a correlation between the political reality and the social dramas through their artistic representation. In every layer of pictorial, or sound, or video matter of his works, the artist turns himself into a sort of archaeologist, able to dig and unveil the ‘ghost’ and unexpected faces of the personal and collective experience: it is as if, together with the artist, the viewer would enter his artworks from the back-door of the memory and have access in this way to a privileged and magical storytelling.</p>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9323c6e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9323c6e\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-696a287 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"696a287\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3082519 elementor-widget-divider--view-line_text elementor-widget-divider--element-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"3082519\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n							<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n			<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n							<span class=\"elementor-divider__text elementor-divider__element\">\n				Education				</span>\n						</span>\n		</div>\n						</div>\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5b42980 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5b42980\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n									<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\"><p>1983 Lithographic Arts Diploma, International School of Graphic Arts Il Bisonte, Florence, Italy.<br />1979 Degree from the Academy of Fine Arts, Florence, Italy.<br />1975 Degree from the Institute of Fine Arts, Baghdad, Iraq.</p></div></div>								</div>\n				</div>\n				</div>\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b51338 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"9b51338\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n		<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-310d379 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"310d379\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n				<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-004ddf5 elementor-widget-di